window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-035", "name_zh": "当下/广阔当下", "name_en": "present / spacious present", "tagline": "赛斯说真正的时间只有一种：广阔到装得下所有过去与未来的当下——你分出的过去、现在、未来，只是它被切成的房间，而你从未离开过它。而它最实用的一层是：威力之点在此刻，你现在的信念正在改写你以为已经定型的过去，和还没发生的未来。", "explanation": "广阔当下（Spacious Present）是赛斯眼中唯一真实的时间：它无始无终、不占空间，内部一切自发而同时地发生，却又包含耐久性。你们以为的过去、现在、未来，只是从它上面切出的保护性隔墙——像房子的墙。一切存有、意识与生命都此刻在其中：未来现在就存在，过去从未被扫走，转世不是接续而是并存。对做人的人来说，现在仍是唯一的立足点：你只能在自己的「现在」里检查、经验、行动，它像一扇窗口，也是心理上的平台。正因如此，赛斯说了那句被引用最多的话：威力之点在于当下。当下的信念会重新改写过去的经验——你一直在改变过去，只是你和它一起变了所以看不出来；同样，你可以从现在开始对一个未来的复原作出反应，插入一个新现在和一个新未来。它的实际意义有两层：理论上，因果论与「最初起源」问题在此失效；实践上，心理时间、情感接纳与对当下的感官沉浸，能让你看穿时间之墙，被目前的状态催眠、以为一切不可能改变才是真正的误区。这个词诞生于早期课第 41 节，从第 44 节起被系统论述，一直延续到晚期口述（第 884–897 节）的「不断创造」模型。", "definitions": [{"zh": "我稍早是在你们的房子附近，所以鲁柏的感觉没有错。他看错了字有一个目的。事实上，在那个情形下，他在潜意识里获得了我的一些思想。而且在之前几分钟就挑选好了，但他的心智在等待着一个合适的机会，来把“广阔”与“现在”连结起来，并重新组合。“广阔的现在”是一个极佳的词语。实际上，只有广阔的现在，因为它是如此的广阔，以你们的说法来讲，你们无法在同一时间里去探索它，所以就试着把它分成过去、现在和未来的较大区块。", "en": "I was about your establishment earlier, and Ruburt was right. There was a purpose in his misreading. Actually, subconsciously he picked up my thoughts on this occasion. He picked them up a few minutes earlier but his mind waited for a suitable occasion to transpose the word spacious in connection with the present. The spacious present is an excellent term. In actuality there is only a spacious present, so spacious that it cannot be explored all at once in your terms, hence your arbitrary division of it into larger rooms of past, present and future.", "source": "Session 41"}, {"zh": "我们广阔的现在包含了所有时间，但它不是一个有别于它们的东西，也不完全是它们的总和，本身始终是展开的、流动的和改变的。", "en": "Our spacious present of which I have spoken contains all times, but it is not a thing apart from them, nor precisely their sum. It is ever unfolding and mobile, and changing itself.", "source": "Session 218"}, {"zh": "广阔的现在是全我存在的基本时间，但自己的不同部分经验着它们自己的时间系统，那是它们感知的独有方式的结果。", "en": "The spacious present is the basic time in which the whole self has its existence, but the various portions of that self have their experience in their own time systems, which are the results of their characteristic methods of perception.", "source": "Session 231"}, {"zh": "即使在我们的讨论中，我们也使用过去、现在和未来这些字眼，但我告诉过你，你的未来可以影响你的过去，广阔的现在是唯一的时间实相。", "en": "Even in our discussions we use the terms past, present and future, but I have told you that your future can influence your past, and that the spacious present is the only time reality.", "source": "Session 249"}, {"zh": "你们的时间显然是一个对广阔的现在所做的诠释，不只所有的创造最初都是由此开始，而且就价值完成而言还一直在继续。", "en": "your time obviously being an interpretation of the spacious present, from which all creation not only originally began but continues in terms of value fulfillment", "source": "Session 109"}, {"zh": "你们的现在，或当下这一刻，是个心理上的平台。似乎宇宙是以某种能量的最初爆炸开始（“大爆炸”论），而进化派却不能解释其原因。许多虔诚的人们相信一个神存在于一个较大的实相次元，他创造了宇宙，而他自身却在其外；他启动了这个创造。许多人跟随上面两种信仰的其中一种，相信不论宇宙的来源为何，这“宇宙”必然会耗尽其能量。已确立的科学十分相信，现在没有能量可被创造或毁灭，而只会转换其形式（如热力学第一定律所述）。科学把能量和物质基本上视为一体，只在不同环境下显现出不同的样子。", "en": "Your now (underlined), or present moment, is a psychological platform. It seems that the universe began with an initial burst of energy of some kind (the “big bang”). Evolutionists cannot account for its cause. Many religious people believe that a god exists in a larger dimension of reality, and that he created the universe while being himself outside of it. He set it into motion. Many individuals, following either persuasion, believe that regardless of its source, the [universe]1 must run out of energy. Established science is quite certain that no energy can now be created or destroyed, but only transformed (as stated in the first law of thermodynamics). Science sees energy and matter as being basically the same thing, appearing differently under varying circumstances.", "source": "Session 882"}, {"zh": "威力之点是在当下。你必须彻底地了解这一点，然后才能把握人生，而开始在所有生活区域里为你的益处用到自然催眠法。它现在已经在你生活中觉得满意的部分使你获益了。", "en": "The point of power is in the present. You must thoroughly understand that, and then you can take hold of your life and begin to use natural hypnosis for your benefit in all areas. It works advantageously for each of you now in those portions of your lives with which you are pleased.", "source": "Session 660"}, {"zh": "过去和现在是同样程度的真实。事实上，有时候过去可以变得比现在更真实，在这样的例子，过去的行动在现在被反应着。你理所当然地认为现在的行动可以改变未来，但现在的行动也可以改变过去。", "en": "In other words the past and the present are real to the same extent. At times in fact the past can become more real than the present, and in such cases past actions are reacted to in the present. You take it for granted that present action can alter the future, but present actions can also alter the past.", "source": "Session 224"}, {"zh": "除非在你的现在，否则你不可能去检查一个原子、一个细胞或任何东西。", "en": "It is impossible for you to examine an atom, a cell, or anything else except in your now.", "source": "Session 684"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "「当下」不只是这一秒：只有一个广阔的现在", "note": "这一块是底图。基本定义在第 41 节给出：「事实上，只有广阔的现在，它是如此的广阔，以你们的说法来讲，你们无法在同一时间里去探索它，所以就试着把它分成过去、现在和未来的较大区块。」同一节连着敲掉两层常识：你们现在就处于它之中，昨天的你们也在，无穷个明天里你们也走不出它；而所有已经存在的东西仍然存在，你们未来将会存在的也已然确实存在。第 231 节把它定位成「全我存在的基本时间」，自己的不同部分却各自经验着自己的时间系统；第 218 节划一条精确的边界：它包含所有时间，但既不是与时间分开的东西，也不完全是它们的总和，「本身始终是展开的、流动的和改变的」。第 109 节直说你们的时间是对广阔的现在所做的一个诠释，一切创造都从它开始、也在它里面继续；第 88 节顺手把潜意识层放进来——所谓潜意识层根本不是一层又一层，而是广阔的现在的一部分；第 249 节留下一句最短的表述：你的未来可以影响你的过去，广阔的现在是唯一的时间实相。\n\n赛斯讲的「当下」远不止日历上的此刻，所以他更常用「广阔的现在」重画时间。既然所有事件都是同时发生的，说「过去的事件导致现在的事件」也就没多大意义。从他自己的位置看这一点更清楚：短期预测最难，因为他无法像你们那样把时间切割到那种程度，相反似乎一瞬间就感知到你们全部的时间片刻（第 411 节）；讲到「四个基石人格」时他也先声明「我现在这样讲只是为了你们的方便而已」（第 303 节）。晚期口述把这条立为定律：不管所有开始与结束、死亡与腐败的表象，所有意识都以一种自发的方式存在于同时性的和谐之中（《未知的实相》卷二第 744 节）。\n\n连这门课自己也住在里面。第 95 节说这些课从来没有在某个特定的时间点开始，也不会结束——「我们在过去、现在和未来都认识彼此，所以这些课存在广阔的现在之中，那样的时间在那里完全没有意义」；第 458 节补一句「媒介即是讯息，每当节目开演的时辰一到，我便在你们的当下这里」。后面所有话都是在这几段上展开的。", "src": "早期课第1册第 41 节；早期课第3册第 88、95、109 节；早期课第5册第 218、231 节；早期课第6册第 249、256 节；早期课第7册第 303 节；早期课第8册第 411 节；早期课第9册第 458 节；《未知的实相卷二》第 744 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 41 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 88 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 109 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 218 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 231 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 249 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 256 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 303 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 411 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 458 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "基本的定义", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0153", "zh": "我稍早是在你们的房子附近，所以鲁柏的感觉没有错。他看错了字有一个目的。事实上，在那个情形下，他在潜意识里获得了我的一些思想。而且在之前几分钟就挑选好了，但他的心智在等待着一个合适的机会，来把“广阔”与“现在”连结起来，并重新组合。“广阔的现在”是一个极佳的词语。实际上，只有广阔的现在，因为它是如此的广阔，以你们的说法来讲，你们无法在同一时间里去探索它，所以就试着把它分成过去、现在和未来的较大区块。", "en": "I was about your establishment earlier, and Ruburt was right. There was a purpose in his misreading. Actually, subconsciously he picked up my thoughts on this occasion. He picked them up a few minutes earlier but his mind waited for a suitable occasion to transpose the word spacious in connection with the present. The spacious present is an excellent term. In actuality there is only a spacious present, so spacious that it cannot be explored all at once in your terms, hence your arbitrary division of it into larger rooms of past, present and future.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0154", "zh": "我再说一遍，只有广阔的现在。你们现在就处于广阔的现在之中。在“你们的昨天”时，你们也是在广阔的现在里，在你们的明天或者无穷尽个明天里，你们也一样无法穿越它。", "en": "Again, there is only the spacious present. You are in the spacious present now. You were in the spacious present in your yesterday and you still will not have traveled through it in your tomorrow, or in eons of tomorrows.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0156", "zh": "在广阔的现在之中，正如它确实存在的样子，所有已经存在的东西仍然存在，所有在你们的未来将会存在的也已然确实存在了。在你们的层面，除非透过一种非常限制的方式，否则你们不能经验这样的实相，而且你们也无法自发地经验这种实相，自发性是广阔的现在的一项特性。以你们伪装时间的观念来看，你们或许会觉得，这些资料听起来很奇怪，令人难以置信。", "en": "In the spacious present as it exists in actuality beyond shadow, all things that have existed still exist, and all things that shall exist in your tomorrow already do exist. You on your plane cannot experience such reality except in a very limited manner, and you cannot experience such reality spontaneously, and spontaneity is the quality of the spacious present. To you with your ideas of camouflage time this material may sound strange and unbelievable.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0286", "zh": "不过，这些所谓的潜意识层，根本不是真的一层又一层，而是广阔的现在的一部分。", "en": "These so-called layers of the subconscious, however, are not really layers at all, but part of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第88节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "88", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0337", "zh": "我们讲过，你们认为它们有最早的起源，发生在你们时间当中特定的某一点，这相对来说是不可能的。内向、个体化、觉察的能量在你们的时间诞生之前就存在，你们的时间显然是一个对广阔的现在所做的诠释，不只所有的创造最初都是由此开始，而且就价值完成而言还一直在继续。在你们的时间诞生之前没有这样的一种发展，说真的，你们的宇宙绝不可能进入存在。", "en": "We have spoken concerning the relative impossibility of first origins as you consider them, occurring at a particular point in your time. Inward, individualized, aware energy existed before the conception of your time, your time obviously being an interpretation of the spacious present, from which all creation not only originally began but continues in terms of value fulfillment. Without such a development before the conception of your time, indeed, your universe would never have come into existence.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0521", "zh": "一号时间不能包含其他的时间，但透过帮助，意识可以某程度察觉到这些其他的时间。而这个感知后来允许了意识逃过时间一的某些禁锢。我说过的，我们广阔的现在包含了所有时间，但它不是一个有别于它们的东西，也不完全是它们的总和，本身始终是展开的、流动的和改变的。", "en": "The number one time cannot contain other times but the consciousness, with help, can to some extent perceive these other times. And this perception then allows consciousness to escape some of the confinements of that one time. Our spacious present of which I have spoken contains all times, but it is not a thing apart from them, nor precisely their sum. It is ever unfolding and mobile, and changing itself.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第218节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "218", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0567", "zh": "就如你所知道的，内在自我存在的时间是广阔的现在。广阔的现在是全我存在的基本时间，但自己的不同部分经验着它们自己的时间系统，那是它们感知的独有方式的结果。", "en": "Now, the time in which the inner ego exists is, as you know, the spacious present. The spacious present is the basic time in which the whole self has its existence, but the various portions of that self have their experience in their own time systems, which are the results of their characteristic methods of perception.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第231节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "231", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0623", "zh": "即使在我们的讨论中，我们也使用过去、现在和未来这些字眼，但我告诉过你，你的未来可以影响你的过去，广阔的现在是唯一的时间实相。", "en": "Even in our discussions we use the terms past, present and future, but I have told you that your future can influence your past, and that the spacious present is the only time reality.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第249节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "249", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "同一层意思的另一批说法", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0638", "zh": "由于所有事件都是同时发生的，所以说过去的事件导致现在的事件，是没有什么意义的。", "en": "Since all events occur at once, there is little to be gained by saying that a past event causes a present event.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第256节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "256", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0731", "zh": "我现在这样讲只是为了你们的方便而已。有四个基石（cornerstone）人格参与了你们的研讨会。现在这些人格的其中三是你的：一个不是你的。按照你们的说法，一个这一次不是“你的”。当你去找而认出时，你就会接受，你现在认不出是你自己的那个自己，是你自己。如果你现在去找，你会认不出你将会认出的自己。因为广阔的现在已经存在，认出这件事已经完成了。你还没有跟上它，你知道。你们是慢郎中。我的朋友鲁柏也是个慢郎中。环境不是在你以为它在的地方。我指的是这些研讨会。按照你们的说法，不“讲话”的声音是你的，但讲师不是你认识的自己。按照你们的说法，它是你还不认识的一个自己。", "en": "I am speaking now for your convenience simply. There are four cornerstone personalities involved in your seminar. Now three of these personalities are yours: one is not yours. One is not“yours\" in your terms as of this time. When you look up and recognize, you will accept that which you do not now recognize as yourself, as yourself. If you looked up now, you would not recognize the self that you will recognize. Because the Spacious present exists as it is, the recognition has already been made. You have not yet caught up with it, you see. You are slowpokes. My friend Ruburt in many respects is also a slowpoke. The environment is not where you think it is. I refer to these seminars. The voice that does not“speak\" in your terms is yours, but the instructor is not yourself as you know yourself. It is a self you do not as yet know in your terms.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第303节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "303", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0859", "zh": "对我来说，短期的预测最困难，因为我无法如你们想的那样，将时间切割到那种程度。相反地，我似乎瞬间就可以感知到你们全部的时间片刻。（停顿） 你们所认识的赛斯能够更清楚感知你们自己的系统。（停顿）从我的角度来看（停顿），我不能像你们那样感知你们的物质世界，但我确实能够感知你们的心灵价值和情感强度，也了解你们只能感知其中极小部分的片段。就像你们将广阔的现在分解成这么多片刻时间然后再去体验一样，你们也将心灵本体、完形，分解成小小的自我结构。", "en": "Short range predictions would be most difficult for me, since I cannot break down time as you think of it to that degree. I perceive instead at one glance seemingly whole segments of your time field. (Pause.) Seth as you knew him perceives your own system more clearly. (Pause.) From my viewpoint (pause) I do not perceive your physical universe then as you do. I do perceive your psychic values and Emotional intensities, and realize that you perceive but very small segments of these. As you break down the spacious present into moments, which you then experience, so also you break down psychic identity, gestalts, into small self structures.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第411节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "411", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1512", "zh": "在此，你们可以看出我们将谈到的是什么。我们的第三个定律是自发性，而不管所有开始与结束、死亡与腐败之表象，所有的意识都以一种自发的方式，以同时性的和谐存在于一个广阔的现在；然而，在广阔的现在之内也有耐久性。", "en": "You may see what we are getting at here. Our third law is spontaneity, and despite all appearances of beginning and end, of death and decay, all consciousnesses exist in the spacious present, in a spontaneous manner, in simultaneous harmony; and yet within the spacious present there is also durability.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "这门课自己也住在广阔的现在里", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0314", "zh": "我在这里要开始结束这一节，但是就像菲利普的宇宙一样，这些课从来没有在特定的时间点开始，早在鲁柏在这个地板踱步之前，他就知道它们了，但他没有觉察到。随着你们改变层面，它们将会结束，或者说它们以你们的说法将会结束，但它们不会结束，因为我们在过去、现在和未来都认识彼此，所以这些课存在广阔的现在之中，这样的时间在那里完全没有意义。", "en": "I will here begin to close the session, though like Philip's universe, the sessions never began at a specific point in time, and Ruburt knew of them long before he paced this floor, though he was not aware of them. And they will end, or they will end in your terms, with your change of planes. But they will not end, and as we have known each other in the past and in the future and in the present, so these sessions exist in the spacious present, where time as such has no meaning.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0950", "zh": "因为，再说一次，在宽阔的当下里，媒介即是讯息；而每当节目开演的时辰一到，我便在你们的当下这里——不论在你们所谓“我的当下”之中我身在何方。", "en": "For again, the medium is the message in the spacious present , and whenever the time for the program arrives I am here in your present, regardless of where I am in what you would term my present.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第458节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "458", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "过去与未来就住在此刻：一切都是同时的", "note": "只有一个当下的话，过去和未来去哪了？全在这里，只是被遮住了。第 131 节说得直白：未来现在就存在，过去从未被一扫而空，在物质场域里你只不过是转头看别处、把焦点从一个点移到另一个点。第 256 节给出尺度：公元前 145 年、公元 145 年、你们过去的与现在的 1000 年——全都当下存在，过去的存在就是现在的存在。第 97 节把它折回每个人自己身上：在广阔的现在里，你已经不是「你将会是」，而是「你已经是的你」，分隔你的只是毫无觉察的面纱。第 249 节拆掉观察的立足点：回望过去就是展望未来，根本没有一个作为基点的「现在」，因为它们本是一体，而你是它的一部分。第 259 节举了个家常例子——五年后你要住的房子还没盖好，「然而，这样一间房子确实有形式，也确实存在广阔的现在之内」；第 290 节连身体都算进去：未来也存在当下的细胞意识中，细胞意识不只存放过去。\n\n如果时间是被切出来的，那「同时」就是常态。第三种内在感官涉及对过去、现在和未来的感知，正是它让内在自我摆脱了连续的因果限制。梦是最容易体验这一点的入口：你可能在「现在」就经验着多年前发生的事件；在梦境状态，那时如现在，所有问题都是同时的，像模型一样摆在那里，人从中挑选要实际经验的事件。赛斯描述那个「可能性的领域」时说得很妙：那里是由所有过去、现在和未来组成的材料库。所以一幅画可以在某个实相里已经完成，而你在当前的架构中却觉得还在等它发展；一个思想可以自行消退再变强，调节它的是自己的本性而不是时间里的规则。心灵与身体也这样运作：细胞带着预知性的知识，现在的行为建立在它上面；心灵多半用联想而不是时间先后组织事件，情感根本不服从时间——只是醒着时你用时间顺序记事情，目前的时刻才整齐地跟着过去的时刻走。结论是双向的：你持续地在改变过去，它看起来没变，是因为你和它一起变了；而「未来」只是事件的另一种深度，事件的根穿过你的过去、现在与未来。他生的记忆一旦浮到表面，就被那个表面渲染，节奏与你现在的节奏并不一致；连转世的档案也仍以另一个可用的「替代的现在」开头。", "src": "早期课第1册第 36 节；早期课第3册第 97、131 节；早期课第5册第 211、234 节；早期课第6册第 249、256、259 节；早期课第7册第 290 节；早期课第8册第 383 节；早期课第9册第 429、472 节；《灵魂永生》第 574 节；《时空之外》第 515 节；《未知的实相卷一》第 681、689 节；《心灵的本质》第 759、787 节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第 806 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 36 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 97 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 131 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 211 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 234 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 249 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 256 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 259 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 290 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 383 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 429 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 472 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 574 节"}, {"n": 14, "id": null, "label": "第 515 节"}, {"n": 15, "id": null, "label": "第 681 节"}, {"n": 16, "id": null, "label": "第 689 节"}, {"n": 17, "id": null, "label": "第 759 节"}, {"n": 18, "id": null, "label": "第 787 节"}, {"n": 19, "id": null, "label": "第 806 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "过去从未被扫走", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0318", "zh": "你忘记了在广阔的现在，你已经不是你将会是，而是你已经是的你。因此，你要投射的这类人格已经被投射了，分隔你的只不过是毫无觉察的这层面纱而已，就像分开两个场域或层面的只不过是毫无觉察的这层面纱一样。", "en": "You forget that in the spacious present you already are not only what you will be, but what you have been. Therefore, such personalities that you would project are already projected, and only the veil of unawareness divides you, as only the veil of unawareness ever separates one field or plane from another.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第97节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "97", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0365", "zh": "在我们过去的课里，我解释过时间的扭曲，而且你们也熟悉广阔的现在。所以，发觉基本上未来现在就存在，过去从未一扫而空，应该不觉得惊讶。在你们的物质场域里，你只不过是转头看别处，或把你的焦点从一个点转到另一个点而已。", "en": "In our past sessions I have explained time distortions, and you are familiar with the spacious present. So it should be no surprise to realize that basically the future is in existence now, and the past has never been swept away. In your physical field you merely look away, or turn your focus from one point to another.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第131节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "131", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0624", "zh": "我们会说出我们要说的话，然后一边进行一边为你理清疑点。现在。回顾过去，现在是按照我的说法，而不是你们的说法，回顾过去必需展望未来，而且你看，没有坚实的基础；没有基本的现在，没有现在这个坚实的基础，由此看到未来或过去。因为它们都是一体的，而你是广阔的现在所属的一部分。", "en": "We will say what we have to say, and then clarify for you later as we go along. Now. To look backward into the past, speaking on my terms now and not yours, to look backward into the past entails looking forward into the future, and there is no firm ground, you see; there is no present in a basic manner, no firm ground that is the present, from which to view the future or the past. For they are all one, and you are a part of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第249节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "249", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0637", "zh": "公元前145年，公元145年，你们过去的1000年、现在的1000年——当下都存在。因此，过去的存在就是现在的存在。换句话说，在广阔的现在之内，你们同时以几个伪装或转世存在着。你们根本不晓得，所谓的过去存在当下，就像所谓的未来存在当下一样，确实无疑。", "en": "A hundred and forty-five B.C., a hundred and forty-five A.D., a thousand years in your past and a thousand years in your present—all exist now. Therefore the past existences are present existences. You exist in other words in several guises or reincarnations, at one time within the spacious present. You simply do not recognize that the so-called past exists now as surely as the so-called future exists now.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第256节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "256", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0651", "zh": "因此，在物质上，你在5年内将要居住的房子，按照你们的说法，现在可能不存在。它可能还没有盖好，因此在物质上你感知不到它。然而，这样一间房子确实有形式，也确实存在广阔的现在之内。", "en": "Physically therefore the house that you will live in within five years may not exist, in your terms, now. It may not have been built yet, therefore physically you do not perceive it. Such a house however does have form, and does exist within the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第259节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "259", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0711", "zh": "未来也存在当下的细胞意识中。当梦与你们所谓尚未变成实质的时间打交道时，自我只不过，再一次，从细胞意识的层面审查它们而已。细胞意识通常被认为单纯只是一个存放处，储存着过去与个人或种族的存在有关的知识而已。然而，因为广阔的现在，所以细胞意识也包含未来的蓝图。", "en": "Now, the future is also present in cellular consciousness. The ego, again, simply censors dreams from the cellular consciousness level when they deal with time that is not yet physical in your terms. Cellular consciousness is usually considered as simply a repository for past knowledge having to do with personal or racial existence. Because of the spacious present however, cellular consciousness also contains blueprints of the future.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第290节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "290", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "同时在场的证据：梦、画、细胞、联想", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0139", "zh": "在我们结束之前，我想提一下第三种内在感官对观念模式（concept patterns）经验的重要性。第三种内在感官，涉及你们称之为过去、现在和未来的感知，它能让内在自我和存有经验直接观念--模式，因此让它们摆脱连续的困果限制。", "en": "Before we close I want to mention the importance of the third inner sense with the experience of concept patterns. The third inner sense, involving what you would call perception of past, present and future, is the sense that enables the inner ego and entities to experience direct concept-patterns, and free them therefore from successive cause and effect limitations.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0502", "zh": "有好几种时间会出现在你的梦中，你必须小心分辨它们。当你正睡着的时候，你可以做一个关于个人过去的梦，在梦里可能会涉及发生在几年前的事件。不过，你可能现在经验着这些发生的事件。", "en": "Now there are several kinds of time, that will appear within your dreams, and you must sort these out carefully. While sleeping in your present time, you may have a dream that concerns your personal past, while the dream is concerned with events that you know to have occurred many years ago. Nevertheless you may experience these events as happening within the present.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第211节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "211", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0580", "zh": "这个可能性的领域，在除了你所熟悉的那个物质系统外播种了很多其他的系统。可能性的领域是由思想印象强而有力地组成的，它没有物质化，但有极逼真和真实的能量储藏。这里的资料是由所有过去、现在和未来所组成的。", "en": "This probable field seeds many other systems beside the one physical system with which you are familiar. The probable field is strongly composed of thought images, not physically materialized, but extremely vivid and actual storehouses of energy. Here is the material from which all pasts and presents and futures are made.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第234节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "234", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0820", "zh": "无论你在意识上是否觉知到这个视觉画面，你都会在意识上觉知到这幅画作。从时间角度看这幅画的人是你，以这种方式感知它的也是你。（珍说话当中坐起来，开始脱下毛衣和鞋子）这幅画是存在的，你在某个实相中已经完成了这幅画。不过，在你当前的架构中，似乎正等待这些事情发展。", "en": "You would have been consciously aware of the painting whether or not you were consciously aware of the vision. It is you who think of the painting in terms of time, and who perceive it in this manner. (Sitting up as she spoke, Jane began to take off her sweater and shoes.) The painting exists and in one reality you have already completed it. In your present framework however you seem to be waiting for the developments to occur.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第383节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "383", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0892", "zh": "一个思想可以很强烈，然后部分消退，再度变强。（停顿。）是它自己的本性在调节它的强度，而不是强度本性中固有的任何规则。这些概念有些很难向你们解释。用你们的话说，那就仿佛你们体验了一个未来的事件，然后一个遥远的过去事件，然后是现在的某一刻。你们不会明白正在发生什么，也看不出其中的内在逻辑。", "en": "A thought can be intense, then partially fade and grow intense again. (Pause.) Its own nature regulates its intensity, rather than any rules inherent in the nature of intensity itself. Some of these concepts are difficult to explain to you. In your terms it would be as if you experienced a future event, then a distant past event, then a moment from the present. You would not understand what was going on, nor see the inner logic within.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第429节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "429", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0973", "zh": "它十分清楚自己不可毁坏，也清楚它的同伴们不可毁坏。建设性的心灵能量若是被故意剥夺了奋发进取的出口，会怎么样？它去弄明白。首当其冲挨攻击是什么滋味？它形成另一个生活情境，然后发现答案。它所能调遣的能量有多强、有多有力？怎样才能最好地运用它？这些问题全都必须得到答案，因为内我是由能量组成的；而在其他活动领域里，思想与情绪会被即刻转化，它们的结果当下可见。那里不像在你们自己的系统之内那样有一个拖延的时间差，也没有你们所知的那种物质身体。", "en": "It knows full well its own indestructibility, and that of its fellows. What happens in the case of constructive psychic energy when it is purposely denied aggressive outlets? It finds out. What does it feel like to be the brunt of aggression? It forms another life situation and discovers the answer. How strong and potent is the energy that is at its command? How can it best be used? It is quite necessary that all of these questions be answered, for the inner self is composed of energy, and in other fields of activity thoughts and emotions are instantaneously translated, their results instantly seen. There is no saving time lag, as within your own system, and there is no physical body such as you know it.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第472节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "472", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1127", "zh": "你明白吗，与此相类还有一个“A-1-b”，仍然由一个可用为许多其他目的的“替代的现在”开始。", "en": "There is an A-1-b, you see, still adjacent to this one, and still starting off from an alternate present that can be used for many other purposes.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第574节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "574", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1173", "zh": "由于你们心理结构的原故使得你们的物质环境呈现出你们今天所见到的外貌。如果你们转而以“观念的联想过程”来感觉自己生命的延续，而不用“自己在时间中过来多少日子”来感觉自己持续的存在，那么你们便可以以一种崭新的角度来感受这个物质世界，你们可以在瞬间认识各种过去现在的事物，并可在事物所显示的各种现象中举一反三。假设：你父亲一生中有八张心爱的椅子，如果你用“领悟后的联想”来当作知觉的工具，而不用时间先后秩序来感觉，那么你能在一瞬间就晓得所有的八张椅子，甚至是只要看到一张便能知道其他的。所以环境不是一个独立于外的东西，它是知觉方式的结果，知觉方式有心灵结构来决定。", "en": "Your own physical environment appears as it does to you because of your own psychological structure. If you gained your sense of personal continuity through associative processes primarily, rather than as a result of the familiarity of self moving through time, then you would experience physical reality in an entirely different fashion. Objects from past and present could be perceived at once, their presence justified through associative connections. Say that your father throughout his lifetime has eight favorite chairs. If your perceptive mechanisms were primarily set up as a result of intuitive association rather than time sequence, then you would perceive all of these chairs at one time; or seeing one, you would be aware of the others. So environment is not a separate thing in itself, but the result of perceptive patterns, and these are determined by psychological structure.", "source": "时空之外 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "515", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1380", "zh": "（“在另一方面来说，如我告诉过你们的，你们持续地改变你们的过去。在你看起来它并没改变，因为你与它一同改变了……你以同样的方式改变你的未来，在这种情形，感知到可能事件的正确频道是必要的——正确是说最后将会被（这个人）选择（来实现）的那个频道。", "en": "“On the other hand, as I have told you, you change your past continually. It does not appear to change to you, for you change with it … You alter your future in the same manner. In such cases it is necessary that the correct channel of probable events be perceived — correct meaning the channel which shall be ultimately chosen [for actualization by the subject] . “These choices, however, are based upon your changing perception of past and present. Because I have a larger scope of perception than you, I can with greater facility predict what may happen. But this is dependent upon my prediction as to which choice [of probable events] you will make, and the choice is still your own … Predictions, per se, do not contradict the theory of free will, though free will is dependent upon much more than any freedom of the ego alone. If the ego were allowed to make all the choices, with no veto power from other layers of the self, you would all be in a sad position indeed.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第681节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "681", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1410", "zh": "从差不多五千万到三千万年前，有数不清的物种，那在你们现在看来会像是突变的物种。在人—动物及动物—人之间的差别不像在你们的时代里这样清楚，在某些方面，意识是更具流动性，较不集中，而且较富实验性的。那早期的亲密、那早期的混杂后来会被记住为在神话里动物形式的神明。这样一种的品种早在你们的古生物学家发现它的确存在之前它就存在了。有过许多制造工具的动物族类，有些比人制造工具的才能还要早，意识知道对它开放的所有成就之可能性。每一种族类在其个人与集体的心灵里都带着这种可能的确实性之蓝图。这些蓝图在生物上是有效的——那是说它们容许了细胞预知性的知识，现在的行为是建立于其上的。这不只是适用于个人，好比说，细胞因此知道它自己将来的样子，而以同样的方式，一整个族类对在它整个的世界环境里它自己“理想的”成就会有无意识的知识。", "en": "From approximately 50 million to 30 million years ago1 there were innumerable species that would now seem to you to be mutated forms. The distinction between man-animal and animal-man was not as clear as it is in your time. In some ways consciousness was more mobile, less centered, and more experimental. That early rapport, that early mixture, would later be remembered in myths of gods in animal form. Such a variety existed long before your paleontologists realize that it did. There were many toolmaking animal species, some predating man’s toolmaking facility. Consciousness knows all of the probabilities of fulfillment open to it. Each species carries in its individual and mass psyche the blueprints of such probable actualities. These blueprints are biologically valid — that is, they allow the cells precognitive knowledge, upon which present behavior is based. This applies not only individually, so that the cell knows its future pattern, for example; but in the same way, an entire species will unconsciously have the knowledge of its own “ideal” fulfillment in its overall world environment.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第689节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "689", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1551", "zh": "不论联想与否，实质上你记住「在时间里」的事件。而目前的时刻利落地追随过去的时刻。不过，心灵多半与联想过程打交道，因而借联想来组织事件，像时间这样的东西在那构架里没有什么意义。可以说，联想是由情感上的经验连接在一起的。广义来说，情感不服从时间。", "en": "Association or no, physically you will remember events in time, with present moments neatly following past ones. The psyche deals largely with associative processes, however, as it organizes events through association. Time as such has little meaning in that framework. Associations are tied together, so to speak, by emotional experience. In a large manner, the emotions defy time.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第759节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "759", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1583", "zh": "在任一特定时间，所有实质经验的成分都呈现在梦境中。然而，实际地说，在任何一个特定时期，人类接受梦的实相的某些部分为其所谓的真实事件，而在那些特殊化的事件周围，形成它「现在」的文明。历史性地说，早期人类梦着飞机和火箭船（Historically speaking, early men dreamed of airplanes and rocket ships.）。就彼而言，他们「自然的电视」在某些方面比你们「技术性的版本」运作得好，因为他们的心象容许他们感知在邻近区域或世界其它部分的事件。不过，他们不能只按个纽按钮就使之发生。心灵的与生物的机制是在那儿，允许人类知道有什么在正常情形下未感知的事件可能会危及其存活，尤其是在紧张或危急的时刻更是如此。但在梦境，那时就如现在，所有这种问题是同时的，像是模型那样，由其中人类于是选择形成它的实质经验的实际事件。", "en": "(Pause at 10:23.) All of the elements of physical experience at any given time are present in the dream state. Practically speaking, however, the species accepts certain portions of dream reality as its so-called real events at any particular time, and about those specialized events it forms its “current” civilizations. Historically speaking, early men dreamed of airplanes and rocket ships. For that matter, their natural television operated better in some ways than your technological version, for their mental images allowed them to perceive events in neighboring areas or in other portions of the world. They could not simply press a button to bring this about, however. The psychic and biological mechanisms were there, permitting the species to know, particularly in time of stress or danger, what normally unperceived events might threaten survival. But in the dream state, then as now, all such issues were contemporary, acting as models from which the species then chose the practical events that formed its physical experience.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第787节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "787", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1625", "zh": "当此种他生记忆真的浮到表面的时候，当然，它就被那个表面所渲染。而它们的节奏与你现在的节奏并不一致，它们并没有像你正常的记忆那样精准的与你的神经系统连接。你的“现在”获得它的深度感就因为那个如你所了解的过去，然而，以某种说法，“将来”代表了属于事件的另外一种深度。一个根向所有的方向发展，事件也是一样，但事件的根经过了你的过去、现在与未来。", "en": "When such other-life memories do come to the surface, they are of course colored by it, and their rhythm is not synchronized. They are not tied into your nervous system as precisely as your regular memories. Your present gains its feeling of depth because of your past as you understand it. In certain terms, however, the future represents, say, another kind of depth that belongs to events. A root goes out in all directions. Events do also. But the roots of events go through your past, present, and future.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第806节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "806", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "自发性与耐久性：两条基本法则", "note": "第 44 节把广阔的现在讲成内在宇宙的法则：自发性是第三条法则，耐久性是第四条——不管开始与结束、死亡与衰败的一切表象，所有意识都以自发的方式存在于广阔的现在、存在于同时的和谐之中；而它之内又有耐久，使它可能且必要的是价值完成与能量转化，两者加起来就是「同时的持久性」，念头本身不经验过去现在未来，却恒久持久。第 51 节澄清最容易误会的一点：这种耐久与通常意义的持续性无关——「持续性」意味着一件事在另一件之前或之后，而广阔的现在里所有发生都是同时的，却又有耐久性。第 41 节补一句：没有连续的片刻点、没有你们的因果关系，一样可以有秩序，而且的确有了秩序。第 137 节落到行动上：所有行动都发生在无限广阔的现在之内，人只是透过放慢对行动的感知，才想像自己延长了时间。", "src": "早期课第1册第 41 节；早期课第2册第 44、51、59 节；早期课第3册第 137 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 41 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 59 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 137 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0160", "zh": "没有一个连续的片刻点，也可以有秩序。没有你们的因果关系，信不信由你，也一样可以有秩序。在自发性里、在广阔的现在的同时性存在里，也可以有秩序，而且的确也有了秩序。", "en": "There can be order without a succession of moments. There can be order, believe it or not, without your cause and effect. There can be order, and there is order, in spontaneity, and in the simultaneous existence of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0167", "zh": "这个值气候的主要属性之一是自发性，它在唯一具有任何真实意义的那种时间的存在之中展现，也就是广阔的现在。", "en": "One of the main attributes of this value climate is spontaneity, that shows itself in the existence of the only sort of time that has any real meaning, that of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0168", "zh": "广阔的现在与耐久性（durability）的存在并不矛盾，而耐久性没有暗含你们以为的一个未来的存在。现在，这看起来可能矛盾，但稍后，我希望你们能更清楚地了解这一点。广阔的现在，虽然自发性地存在、虽然同时发生，但在它之内仍包含耐久的（duration）性质。", "en": "The spacious present does not contradict the existence of durability, but durability does not imply the existence of a future as you conceive it. Now this may appear contradictory, but later I hope that you will understand this more clearly. The spacious present, while existing spontaneously, while happening simultaneously, still contains within it qualities of duration.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0169", "zh": "一个念头本身并没有觉察到，比方说，过去、现在和未来，而且虽然它没有经历现在、过去和未来，但它仍然恒久持久。包括在广阔的现在之中的持久，也完全没有意味着，就比方说为了达到成熟，而禁止成长而言的一种暂停。", "en": "An idea is not itself aware of past, present and future for example, and yet having no experience with present, past and future, it still endures. Nor does the duration involved in the spacious present in any way involve a suspension in terms of, for example, growth forbidden to achieve maturity.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0170", "zh": "能量转换与价值完成，都存在于广阔的现在之中，加起来成为一种同时也是自发的持久性。能量转换与价值完成加起来就等于是一种同时的持久性。", "en": "Energy transformation and value fulfillment, all existing within the spacious present, add up to a durability that is at the same time spontaneous. Energy transformation and value fulfillment add up to a durability that is simultaneous.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0171", "zh": "这里，你可能看出我们正要讨论什么了。我们的内在宇宙第三条基本法则是自发性（spontaneity），不管开始和结束的所有表象，也不管死亡与衰败的所有表象，所有的意识都以自发的方式存在于广阔的现在之内，存在于同时的和谐之中，然而，在广阔的现在之内也有面耐久性。", "en": "You may see what we are getting into here. Our third law is spontaneity, and despite all appearances of beginning and end, despite all appearances of death and decay, all consciousness exists in the spacious present, in a spontaneous manner, in simultaneous harmony, and yet within the spacious present there is also durability.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0172", "zh": "耐久性（Durability）是我们内在宇宙的第四条基本法则。要不是因为价值完成和能量转化，在广阔的现在的架构之内，就不会存在耐久性。这两者使得在广阔的现在之内的耐久性不仅可能，而且必要。", "en": "Durability is our fourth law. Durability within the framework of the spacious present would not exist were it not for the laws of value fulfillment and energy transformation. These make duration within the spacious present not only possible but necessary.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0206", "zh": "就“持续性”这个词的一般用法而言，它是没有持续性的。“持续性”通常隐含一件事发生在另一件之前或之后的意思。广阔的现在反而包含自发性，而且在它之内，所有的发生都是同时的，但又有耐久性。", "en": "It does not have continuity, in the manner in which the term continuity is usually used. Continuity usually implies one thing happening before or after another. The spacious present contains instead spontaneity, and within it all happenings are simultaneous, and yet there is durability.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0378", "zh": "透过减慢他对行动的感知，人类想像他延长了时间。这当然不是事实。他只不过成功地感知到行动的零星片段，抗拒它的流动而已。一方面，行动的确是同时发生的，但所有的行动全都包含在其中，因为它发生在无限广阔的现在之内。在梦中，行动被赋予更多的自由，得以比较不受阻碍地流动。", "en": "By slowing down his perception of action, man imagines that he lengthens time. This of course is not the case. He merely succeeds in perceiving action as bits and pieces, and fights its flow. On the one hand action is indeed simultaneous, yet in it all action is contained, for it occurs within the unlimited spacious present. In dreams action is given more freedom, and allowed to flow in a less hampered fashion.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第137节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "137", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "品质-深度：它给当下加的那个维度", "note": "第 59 节的补充维度：品质-深度像一阵吹过广阔现在的风，赋予它真正令人惊奇的维度。赛斯自己承认这类概念最难转译成字句，不喜抽象的读者可以跳过这两段。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0225", "zh": "如果你想知道，品质-深度就是在心理实相的价值气候之内运作，赋予广阔的现在真正令人惊奇的维度，而广阔的现在包含在心理实相价值气候之内。", "en": "Now if you wish, Quality-depth operates within the value climate of psychological reality, and gives truly amazing dimension to the spacious present, which is contained within the value climate of psychological reality.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0226", "zh": "如果你希望，可以把品质-深度原理想成是一阵吹过广阔的现在的风，它的确就像是一阵风，因为它之所以为人所知是因为它的效应；如果你一定要从视角上想像它的画面，那么它也许有一个漏斗的外形。所有这些观念最难转译成字句。", "en": "You may if you wish consider the Quality-depth principle as blowing like a wind through the spacious present, it indeed being like a wind in that it is known by its effects; and if you must think of it visually it would, perhaps, have a funnel shape. All of these concepts are most difficult to translate into word patterns.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "无始无终：因果论在这里失效", "note": "三处最狠的断言：第 41 节——没有开始也没有结束，那只是你们的伪装概念结构给出的幻觉，所有存在的层面都在广阔的现在里有它们的存在，所有片段体的梦都在同一时间上演；第 95 节——广阔的现在不知道有开始和结束，构成万物的能量永远不可能被撤回，任何曾经存在过的东西都不可能脱离存在，只是改变形式；第 51 节——当自发性被真正了解，建立在持续性上的因果论就「站不住脚」。起源问题上，第 107、109 节说你们的时间里没有最初的起源点，「内在来自它自己」，在广阔的现在里连「过去」都不存在，未来以那些字眼来说也不存在。第 54 节用实例收口：「你们星球诞生前就有一批存有」与「新的存有正在形成」这对矛盾，只在你们的时间架构里才成立——在广阔的现在的架构里，这一切都是自发的。", "src": "早期课第1册第 41 节；早期课第2册第 51、54 节；早期课第3册第 95、107、109 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 41 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 54 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 107 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 109 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0161", "zh": "秩序是一切实相最基本的属性之一，并且秩序是一切事物的固有属性。没有开始也没有结束；只有你们的伪装概念结构给出的这种幻觉。所有存在的层面，有它们的存在（being）在在广阔的现在里，而所有片段体的梦也都在同一时间上演。", "en": "Order is one of the most basic attributes of all reality, and order is an inherent attribute in all things. There is no beginning and no end; only your camouflage idea structures give this illusion. All planes of existence have their being in the spacious present, and all fragment dramas are acted at the same time.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0205", "zh": "回来稍微说一下，我想再提提我们广阔的现在，一切万物在其中都有它们的存在。一旦这广阔的现在，带着它的自发性（spontaneity）被了解了，因果论就会落幕。持续性（continuity）造成的因果论，是站不住脚的。基本上，你们知道，广阔的现在的确有耐久性（durability），因为有价值完成的存在。", "en": "Now returning briefly, I would like again to mention our spacious present, in which all things have their existence. When the spacious present is understood, with its attributes of spontaneity, then the cause and effect theory will fall. The cause and effect theory being the result of continuity holds no water. Basically, the spacious present as you know does have durability, because of the existence of value fulfillment.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0215", "zh": "我也曾说过，新的存有正在形成，但是在广阔的现在架构里，这一切都是自发的。这个矛盾只有就你们的角度来说似乎才是一个矛盾。在我看来一点也不矛盾。为了实际的目的，你们也许可以说，就你们来说确实是，存有有的是时间去发展更多的人格。但我要你们了解，这只有在你们自己的时间架构内才是真的。", "en": "I also said that new entities were being formed, but in the framework of the spacious present all this is spontaneous. The contradiction seems a contradiction only on your terms. On my terms there is none. For practical purposes you may say, in truth on your own terms, that entities simply have had time to develop further personalities. But I want it understood that this is true only within your own time framework.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0310", "zh": "我也说过，广阔的现在不知道有开始和结束，而且构成万物的那股能量永远不可能被撤消。个体化的能量也不可能丧失它的个体性，而且就非常实际的意义来说，任何曾经存在过的东西都不可能脱离存在，而只是改变它的形式。", "en": "Also I mentioned that the spacious present knows no beginning or end, and that energy, of which everything is composed, can never be withdrawn. Nor can individualized energy ever lose its individuality, nor in a very actual sense can anything which has ever existed go out of existence, but merely change its form.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0333", "zh": "在你们所知的时间里，根本没有最初的起源点，因为在广阔的现在里，过去并不存在，就像未来以那些字眼来说也不存在。在广阔的现在里，梦世界与未伪装的经验有着更紧密的连结，但在一个伪装的视角内，它依然和可以辨认的物质实相投射打交道。", "en": "In time as you know it, there simply is no point of first origin, since in the spacious present the past does not exist, as the future does not exist in those terms. The dream world is more closely connected with uncamouflaged experience in the spacious present, but it still is in a camouflage perspective, dealing with recognizable projections of material reality.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第107节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "107", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0338", "zh": "对那些质问那股内在能量起源的人，你可以跟他们说，内在来自它自己。在广阔的现在之中，根本没有过去。在时间当中不可能有任何你们感知得到的起源点。这个看法只有在你们的伪装视角之内才看似合乎逻辑，但这并不代表，你们仍然无法利用自己的内在经验领会它的一些意义。", "en": "To those who ask concerning the origin of that inward energy you may say that the inwardness came from itself. In the spacious present there simply is no past. There can be no point of origin in time as you conceive it. It is only within your camouflage perspective that this remark appears illogical, but this does not mean that you still cannot grasp some of its meaning, using your own inner experience.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第109节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "109", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "比喻：墙、画、森林、方块", "note": "广阔的现在有耐久却不占空间，语言用尽时赛斯借画面说话。墙（第 41 节）：过去/现在/未来的隔墙就像房子的墙，是一种保护性伪装，让你不必面对还没有能力处理的内在力量与实相。画（第 44 节）：画中距离看似不断向背景延伸、却永远触及不到画的后方——有耐久性却不占空间的直觉模型。森林（第 54 节）：树是意识，全都同时存在，整座森林就是广阔的现在，而它不占你们以为的空间。方块（第 45 节）：你们只能在最贴近自己的方块里看到它的一小块，还把它看成过去/现在/未来的伪装波浪。巨人影像（第 429 节）：把一个类人存有的形象投射到午夜星空，它边界内的无数行星与恒星就是片刻点——既是它身体的细胞，也是它穿行经验的心理门户；那里总有与你们「持续性」观念相应的东西，但那其实是强度的问题。第 101 节提醒这些图的边界：在整体存在于广阔现在之内的维度里，宽高长和时间参照点都毫无意义。", "src": "早期课第1册第 41 节；早期课第2册第 44、45、54 节；早期课第3册第 101 节；早期课第9册第 429 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 41 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 45 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 54 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 101 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 429 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0157", "zh": "我说过，你们房子的墙壁，实际上并不是那样子存在，而你们对广阔的现在的划分也一样不存在。你们外在感官体验到房子的墙壁，而墙壁提供了保护，使你们可以抵挡其他具体化的伪装物，甚至遮风、避雨、防寒等等；同样地，你们自己建造出来的过去、现在与未来的隔墙，也是另一种不同的伪装物，用来保护你们，使你们不会面对到内在的力量与实相，因为这些内在力量与实相，你们还没有足够的能力可以处理。", "en": "As I have said that the walls of your house do not actually exist as such, so the divisions that you have placed within the spacious present do not exist. But as the walls of your house are experienced by your outer senses, and serve to protect you against other camouflage materializations, even those of wind and rain and cold, so do the walls of past, present and future, erected by you as a different kind of camouflage pattern, protect you from inner forces and realities with which you are not as yet equipped to deal.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0174", "zh": "不过，请记住，我们的宇宙充满它自己却不占用任何空间，还有我们那幅想像的画，画中的距离看起来在背景里一直不断延伸，却永远不会触及画的后方，这也许可以让你们对我们那广阔的现在有一些直觉的了解，它有着耐久性却不占用任何空间。", "en": "Remember however our universe that fulfills itself yet takes up no space, and our imaginary painting in which distance appears ever further in the background, while never touching the back of the painting, and this may give you some intuitive understanding of our spacious present that has duration, and yet takes up no space.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0177", "zh": "如果他们够幸运，能穿透他们自己的方块，我怀疑他们做得到，他们也只会发现最靠近他们的方块，而无从想像真的有无数这样的方块。广阔的现在的一小部分，出现在了你们的方块里，但你们看到的它却是伪装的持续，是过去、现在和未来的伪装波浪。", "en": "If they were ever lucky enough to pierce through their own cube, which is doubtful, they would merely discover the cube nearest to them, without ever imagining that there were literally numberless such cubes. A small portion of the spacious present appears in your cube but you see it in camouflage terms of continuity, in camouflage waves of past, present and future.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第45节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "45", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0212", "zh": "我们带着这个比喻再向前一大步。现在，如果你能想象的话，我们称这整座森林为广阔的现在。把树比作为意识，全都同时存在；而广阔的现在这座森林并不占用你们认为的空间。", "en": "We will carry this analogy a giant step further. Now we will call the whole forest, if you can conceive of it, the spacious present. The trees are compared to consciousnesses, all existing simultaneously; and yet this forest of spacious present does not take up space, as you think of space.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0325", "zh": "宽度、高度、长度，在你们所知的空间中没有存在的维度里，毫无意义。作为参考点的时间，在一个整体存在于广阔的现在之内的维度中，毫无意义。", "en": "Width, height, length have no meaning in dimensions that do not have existence in space as you know it. Time as a reference point has no meaning in a dimension that has its existence wholly within the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第101节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "101", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0890", "zh": "现在。如同我告诉过你们的，有某种持续性。无论如何，在广阔的现在之内，总有与你们关于持续性的观念相应的东西；然而那其实是强度的问题。存有本身就由这样的强度组成。只是为了类比起见，想象一个巨大化的存有形象——一个类人的形象——铺展在你们物质宇宙里的任何地方。而如果这形象被投射到午夜的星空上，那么在它看似的边界之内，你们便会看到无数的行星与恒星。让这些代表片刻点。一方面，它们是存有的一部分，就如你们的细胞是你们身体的一部分。另一方面，存有的意识能够穿行于其中。它们是他自己心理构成之内的门户，通往种种经验。", "en": "Now. As I have told you, there is duration of a kind. What would correspond, in any case, to your idea of duration within the spacious present ; it is a matter of intensities however. Now the entity is in itself composed of such intensities. Simply for the sake of analogy, imagine the image, a humanoid one, of an entity giant-sized, spread out anywhere in your physical universe. And if the image were projected against a midnight sky, within its apparent boundaries then you would see a multitude of planets and stars. Let these represent moment points. On one hand they are a part of the entity, as your cells are a portion of your body. On the other hand the entity’s consciousness can travel through these. They are doorways within his own psychological makeup, into experiences.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第429节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "429", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "与「片刻点」「心理时间」的分工", "note": "这一层道理和另外两个概念高度相邻，分工在原文里就写明了。片刻点是广阔当下的一部分：第 151 节说片刻点本身就是任意界定的、一种人工的区分，实际上是由你们在当下框架内能够吸收的行动数量组成——「片刻点实际上是广阔现在的一部分」；第 219 节接着说，片刻点是广阔现在较大部分的一个小小实现，梦里的自我从「时间是一串片刻」解脱之后，自己的其他部分就能穿行于这些片刻点。心理时间是靠近它的实践杠杆：第 41 节说心理时间「几乎可以让你们拥有广阔的现在的自由」，帮你们看穿过去与未来之间的墙。教学次序上，第 241 节赛斯自己承认：不把广阔的现在先讲清楚，根本没法向你们解释片刻点。第 151 节把潜意识也接上：广阔的现在之内没有真正的过去现在未来，潜意识向内向外都延伸、包覆无数片刻点——对内在自我的很多部分而言，你们所谓的「一个片刻」几乎是无可限量的片刻。", "src": "早期课第1册第 41 节；早期课第4册第 151 节；早期课第5册第 219 节；早期课第6册第 241 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 41 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 241 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0162", "zh": "这个资料的某些部分，需要一定的时间来适应，但我想现在就把这部分提供给你们；也许你们会看到，运用心理时间对于你们有多么重要。心理时间几乎可以让你们拥有广阔的现在的自由。有关这方面，我后面还会说更多，但是你们心理时间的经验，某程度上，将会帮助你们看穿过去与未来之间的墙。我知道，由于你们自己层面之中情境的关系，你们对于“没有开始也没有结束”这句话，几乎无法理解，而这一部分也已经被知道有好几世纪了。你们自己爱因斯坦的理论，将会助上一臂之力，使这种观念在科学上占有重要地位。", "en": "Some of this material will take some getting used to but I wanted to give it to you now; and perhaps you will see how important the use of psychological time can be to you. It comes very close to allowing you the freedom of the spacious present. There is more I will say later along these lines, but your experience with psychological time will to some degree help you to see through the walls of past and future. I realize you will find the statement, there is no beginning or end, almost incomprehensible, because of your own situation on your own plane, and yet this has been known for centuries; and your own Einstein’s theories will help to give the idea scientific respectability.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0399", "zh": "对于我们才开始触及的很多主题，要解释的还很多，因为所有东西都相互关联；我们谈过的片刻点、广阔的现在，以及全我当中你们称之为潜意识的那一部分之间，的确有关联。", "en": "There is much to be explained along many lines which we have only begun to touch upon, for all things are correlated; and there is indeed a correlation between our moment points of which we have spoken, the spacious present, and that portion of the whole self which you call the subconscious.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0400", "zh": "原则上我们这里主要是在探讨行动的本质，而且实质上所有表面的区分都是为了解释而任意为之。片刻点本身就是任意界定的，是一种人工的区分。我们说过，对你们来说，片刻点其实是由你们在当下的架构之内能够吸收的行动数量所组成，因为片刻点实际上是广阔现在的一部分。", "en": "We are dealing here principally, and in the main, with the essence of action, and essentially all apparent divisions are arbitrary for the sake of explanation. The moment point is in itself arbitrary, an artificial division. As we have said, the moment point for you is actually composed of the amount of action which you are capable of assimilating within your present framework, for the moment point is indeed a portion of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0401", "zh": "潜意识既向外延伸也向内延伸，在广阔的现在之内没有真正的过去、现在和未来，所以的确有无限的内在和外在；而且再一次，行动之内的行动也是无限的，这些行动永无止境，因为它们是自生的。所以，内我的其他部分甚至向四面八方延伸得更远，因此包覆很多片刻点。于是，对内我的很多部分而言，你们所谓的一个片刻，就相当于一个几乎无可限量的片刻，因为没有了经验，没有了行动，连物理时间都毫无意义。", "en": "The subconscious, reaching outward, reaches also inward. For while there is no real past or present or future within the spacious present, there is indeed an infinity of inward and outward; and again, of actions within actions, and there is no end to these actions for they are self-generating. The other portions of the inner self reach then even further in all directions, and they therefore envelop many moment points. To many portions of the inner self then, what you would call a moment would correspond to an almost limitless number of moments, for even physical time has no meaning without experience without action.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0530", "zh": "我们再次开始谈我们的片刻点。现在，这个出现在你们物质宇宙的片刻点，是这个广阔的现在较大部分的一个小小实现。在梦的状态，当自我从时间是一系列的片刻这种概念里解脱出来，那自己的其他部分可以旅行过这些片刻点，然后在这里，你会开始一趟和你的概念中的时间空间无关的、穿越深度的旅行。", "en": "We start once more with our moment point. For now this moment point which appears within your physical universe is but a small materialization of larger portions of the spacious present. In the dreaming state, when the ego is released from its idea of time as a series of moments, then other portions of the self can travel through these moment points, and you have here a journey through depths that have nothing to do with your （underline your） concept of time or space.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0601", "zh": "例如，直到我清楚说明广阔的现在这个观念之前，我无法向你解释片刻点。这并不像它表面看起来那么简单，因为其中不涉及任何强制，所以鲁柏向来都是同意让我把概念塞给他，而他在我的协助下以说话的方式解读。", "en": "I could not have explained moment points to you, for example, until I had clearly given the idea of the spacious present. It is not as simple a thing as it might seem, for there is no coercion involved, Ruburt always consenting to let me push concepts at him, which he interprets speech-wise with my assistance.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第241节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "241", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "一切都是同时的，为什么还盯着当下：它是唯一的立足点", "note": "既然一切都是同时的，为什么反复强调「当下」？因为对做人的人来说，现在是你唯一的操作台。赛斯说过一句很硬的话：你不可能去检查一个原子、一个细胞或任何东西——除非在你的现在。一部分的你确实「受限于现在的时间」，而这恰恰是这套装置的用意：自我意识要等现在的经验积累得够广，才到得了能接受更多资料的阶段。你目前认同的就是这个现世的自我，所以一想到死后生活，你其实想的是这个自我的未来生活——而更大的多次元知识，其实一直就在你现在意识活动的背后。这个操作台具体长什么样：你存在的活力经由你「现在」这扇窗口进入三度空间，每个「现在」都会被充电、充满潜能，自己之内因此形成作为吸引力的「最高点」，存有被放大了的潜能经由它流过。而你的「现在」本身是心理上的平台——不是一条流走就没了的河面，而是站得住的地方。甚至回头看转世，最终受惠的也是当下的这个意识自我：那些无法解释的倾向与习性，会被看成整体模式的一部分。", "src": "早期课第5册第 220 节；早期课第7册第 312 节；《灵魂永生》第 547、585 节；《个人实相的本质》第 668 节；《未知的实相卷一》第 684、686 节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第 882 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 220 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 312 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 547 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 585 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 668 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 684 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 686 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 882 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0533", "zh": "不过，他感知到一部分的你是受限于你现在的时间，这对他而言是最不能理解的。", "en": "He perceived that a portion of you was bound, however, within your present time, and this was almost incomprehensible to him.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第220节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "220", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0756", "zh": "各个转世的自己在表面上（划线）都可以被当成是一整个字谜拼图的一部分，因为它们全部都是整体的一分子；但是它们可以从整体散开，分别存在，虽然它们的意义也跟着减小。就全我来说，自己的各个部分之间是有沟通的。未来的自己与过去的自己往来。彻底了解转世的存在对当下有意识的自己是有好处的。无法解释的倾向和习性于是被看成是一个整体模式的一部分。", "en": "The various reincarnated selves can be superficially (underlined) regarded as portions of a whole crossword puzzle for they are all portions of the whole; and yet they can exist scattered from the whole, although their meaning is then diminished. In the case of the whole self there is communication between various portions of the self. Future and past selves mingle. A thorough understanding of reincarnated existences are of benefit to the conscious present self. Unexplained tendencies and inclinations then are seen as part of an overall pattern.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第312节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "312", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1059", "zh": "首先你必须了解的是，你现在并不知你真正的本体，反倒与你目前的自我认同，因此当你想到所谓死后的生活时，你实际上是指你所知的自我的未来生活。在轮回结束时，你十分透彻地了解你的基本本体、你存在的内核是比你所有转世人格的总和还要广大的。", "en": "First of all you must understand, again, that now you do not realize your true identity. You identify instead with your present ego, so when you think in terms of life after death you really mean a future life of the ego that you know. At the end of the reincarnational cycle you understand quite thoroughly that you, the basic identity, the inner core of your being, is more than the sum of your reincarnational personalities.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第547节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "547", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1150", "zh": "在“全我”之内永远有内在的觉悟。每个人心内均理解“所有存在的意义”。对“多次元存在”的知识不只是在你现在有意识活动的背后，而且每个人内心也知道，他有意识的生命是依赖着一个更大的确实的次元。这更大的次元无法在一个三次元的系统里具体化，但对这更大次元的知识由“存在”的最深心处泛滥流出，向外投射，改变它所触及的一切。", "en": "There are internal realizations always present within the whole self. There is comprehension of the meaning of all existence within each personality. The knowledge of multidimensional existence is not only in the background of your present conscious activity, but each man knows within himself that his conscious life is dependent upon a greater dimension of actuality. This greater dimension cannot be materialized in a three-dimensional system, yet the knowledge of this greater dimension floods outward from the innermost heart of being, and is projected outward, transforming all it touches.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第585节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "585", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1343", "zh": "这些都是经由你“现在”的这个窗口而发生。再次说明，就能量而言，你存在的活力侵入三度空间的实相里，而形成一个粒子，那即是你现在的“这个人”。但这个粒子也以有节奏的模式从地球折射开。这也对着你自己的其他部分在时空连续的其他点发生，但每隔一段时间，你们就会相遇，可以这样说。你们的每一个“现在”在相遇时都会被充了电，而充满了潜能；你的存在——它本身是有意识的能量——也被你的各种经验及它自己“过去”组合与放大的力量所丰富。因此，在每一个“自己”之内形成了最高点。而这些被作为吸引力的“最高点”，现在被打开来，而通过它，这个“存在”被放大了的潜能可以流过。然而这些可能看起来像是反复无常的能量，可以用“太阳黑子”来做比喻。从心理上来说，发生了伟大的发酵，而常常所涉及的个别人格会顺着新方向去组织他们自己。", "en": "All of this happens through the window of your present. In terms of energy, again, the vitality of your entity impinging into three-dimensional reality forms a particle that is your present being. But this particle is also deflected away from the earth in a rhythmic pattern. The same happens to other portions of your self at other points in the space-time continuum, but at certain intervals you meet, so to speak. Each of your “presents” becomes charged, filled with potentiality; and your entity, itself conscious energy, is also enriched by your various experiences, by the combined and magnified power of its own “past.” Apexes are therefore formed within each self. These apexes serve as attractions, now opened, through which the magnified potency of the entity can flow. This may appear as erratic energy, however, an analogy being sunspots. Psychologically, great ferment occurs, and often the individual personalities involved organize themselves along new lines.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第668节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "668", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1390", "zh": "除非在你的现在，否则你不可能去检查一个原子、一个细胞或任何东西。因为你的感官经验跟随着一个你能了解的时间模式，于是你认为当然，好比说，一个细胞是其过去之结果，而它现在的状况是由那过去升起的。胎儿长成为一个成人，并非因为它是由过去被设定程式的，而是因为它多少预知性的觉察到其可能性，而然后由那“未来”把这资料印入那过去的结构里。", "en": "It is impossible for you to examine an atom, a cell, or anything else except in your now. Period. Because your sense experience follows a time pattern that you can understand, then you take it for granted that a cell, for example, is the result of its past, and that its present condition arises from the past.4 The fetus grows into an adult, not because it is programmed from the past, but because it is to some extent precognitively aware of its probabilities, and from the “future” then imprints this information into the past structure.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第684节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "684", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1400", "zh": "心灵认识它自己，而且觉察到它的各个部分。当自我意识达到了生物上与精神上的能力之某一点时，当现在的经验变得够广时，那时，自我意识就会在一个它可以开始接受更多资料的阶段了。的确，它现在就在那个阶段了。", "en": "The psyche knows itself and is aware of its parts. When ego consciousness reached a certain point of biological and mental competence, when experience in the present became extensive enough, then ego consciousness would be at the stage where it could begin to accept greater data. Indeed, it is now at that stage.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第686节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "686", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1650", "zh": "你们的现在，或当下这一刻，是个心理上的平台。似乎宇宙是以某种能量的最初爆炸开始（“大爆炸”论），而进化派却不能解释其原因。许多虔诚的人们相信一个神存在于一个较大的实相次元，他创造了宇宙，而他自身却在其外；他启动了这个创造。许多人跟随上面两种信仰的其中一种，相信不论宇宙的来源为何，这“宇宙”必然会耗尽其能量。已确立的科学十分相信，现在没有能量可被创造或毁灭，而只会转换其形式（如热力学第一定律所述）。科学把能量和物质基本上视为一体，只在不同环境下显现出不同的样子。", "en": "Your now (underlined), or present moment, is a psychological platform. It seems that the universe began with an initial burst of energy of some kind (the “big bang”). Evolutionists cannot account for its cause. Many religious people believe that a god exists in a larger dimension of reality, and that he created the universe while being himself outside of it. He set it into motion. Many individuals, following either persuasion, believe that regardless of its source, the [universe]1 must run out of energy. Established science is quite certain that no energy can now be created or destroyed, but only transformed (as stated in the first law of thermodynamics). Science sees energy and matter as being basically the same thing, appearing differently under varying circumstances.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第882节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "882", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "威力之点在于当下：现在的信念改写过去与未来", "note": "这是整条概念里最出名、也最实用的一段。正式的讲法在第 224 节：过去和现在是同样程度的真实，有时候过去甚至比现在更真实，那样的例子里过去的行动在现在被反应着——你理所当然地认为现在的行动只能改变未来，但它同样能改变过去。当下之所以威力大，是因为信念在这里与物质碰头：第 654 节教你把注意力持续放在自己视为「潜在」的能力上，那些能力就会在你的目前变得突出，而「当下的信念，会重新改写而改变过去的经验」——不只是被遗忘的、无意识感知的事件会以新的方式重新组织，身体对那些「过去」事件的整个反应都会变。反过来也一样：几乎所有目前缺陷的案例，都是当事人教会了自己去强调负面的一面（第 657 节）；现在的念头还会唤醒细胞里一直存着的旧印记，等于用现在给过去重新通电（第 633 节）。这一点也测得到：公寓在两点时舒适、温馨、宁静，二十分钟后忽然显得拥挤杂乱，那不是想象——你已经改变了当下存在于周遭物质环境内的关系，并且在物质上感受到这种变化（第 338 节）。赛斯把这一点用得很接地气：在信巫术的文化里，医生揭出一个「诅咒」，然后用当下的威力点把它反转掉（第 659 节）；连他自己的转世版本都说，鲁柏用更大的知识改变着当前的实相，而他目前的经验也改变着赛斯目前的经验，两者之间有无穷尽的交流（第 728 节）。落到病房里也一样：你可以现在开始对一个未来的复原作出反应（《神奇之道》第 13 节）；梦显示旧信念被剪掉，等于插入一个新现在和一个新未来（《健康之道》第 2 节）。", "src": "早期课第5册第 224 节；早期课第8册第 338 节；《个人实相的本质》第 633、654、657、659 节；《未知的实相卷二》第 728 节；《神奇之道》第 13 节；《健康之道》第 2 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 224 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 338 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 633 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 654 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 657 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 659 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 728 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 13 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 2 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0549", "zh": "换句话说，过去和现在是同样程度的真实。事实上，有时候过去可以变得比现在更真实，在这样的例子，过去的行动在现在被反应着。你理所当然地认为现在的行动可以改变未来，但现在的行动也可以改变过去。", "en": "In other words the past and the present are real to the same extent. At times in fact the past can become more real than the present, and in such cases past actions are reacted to in the present. You take it for granted that present action can alter the future, but present actions can also alter the past.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第224节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "224", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0781", "zh": "举例来说，假如你的公寓在两点时看起来很舒适、温馨、宁静，20分钟后突然变得拥挤、不舒服和杂乱，那么你会发现这不是想象。你已经改变了当下存在于周遭物质环境内的关系，而你也感受到这种物质上的变化。", "en": "If, for example, at two o'clock your apartment appears comfortable, cozy and peaceful and twenty minutes later it suddenly seems crowded, uncomfortable and cluttered, then you see this is not imagination. You have changed the relationships existing within the immediate physical environment, and you perceive the change physically.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第338节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "338", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1205", "zh": "你的思想会启动适当的感觉。然而，在你的觉察之外，它们也会触发那些事发生当时，细胞受到刺激而后留下的那个永恒不朽的记忆。到某个程度，一个细胞的回忆被重新播放了——而对整个身体而言，承认了它在那时候的情况。", "en": "Your thoughts will activate the appropriate feelings. Beneath your awareness, however, they will also trigger the cells’ ever-present memory imprints of stimuli received when those events occurred. There is, to some extent now, a cellular memory playback — and on the part of the entire body, the recognition of its state at that time.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第633节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "633", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1260", "zh": "在日常的实际经验里，试着对似乎是次要的能力——那些你认为是潜在的——集中精神一会儿。如果用你的想象力和意志持续这样做，那么，那些能力在你的目前会变得突出。当下的信念，会重新改写而改变过去的经验。不只是过去的、被遗忘的及无意识感知的事件，会以新的方式被放在一起，并在新的主题下组织起来，而且在那个过去（那是现在不可感知的），身体对似乎是过去事件的整个反应会改变。 （虽然有很多的停顿，却非常有力地：）", "en": "In daily practical experience, try to concentrate for a while upon seemingly subordinate abilities, ones that you think of as latent. If you do so consistently, using your imagination and will, then those abilities will become prominent in your present. The current beliefs will reprogram and alter past experience. It is not simply that past, forgotten, unconsciously perceived events will be put together in a new way and organized under a new heading, but that in that past (now not perceivable), the entire bodily response to seemingly past events will change.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第654节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "654", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1288", "zh": "在几乎所有关于目前缺陷的案例里，在那个特定区域有一个重要的问题：这个人不管因为什么理由，曾经教他自己去强调“负面的”观点。", "en": "In almost all cases of present limitation, there is one main theme in that particular area: The individual has schooled himself or herself to stress “negative” aspects, for whatever reasons.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第657节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "657", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1315", "zh": "如果这个文化的观念包括巫毒（Voodoo）或巫术，那么，人们就会在那个范围里去看整个治疗的情况，而发现一个诅咒；然后用当下的威力点，医生就可以把它反转过来。", "en": "If the cultural concepts include voodoo or witchcraft, then the therapeutic situation will be seen in that context, and a curse uncovered; which, using the power point of the present, the doctor will then reverse.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第659节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "659", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1483", "zh": "我有身为鲁柏的记忆——但我曾是的鲁柏并非在他的实相里现在的鲁柏。他令我惊奇，而他的反应改变了我的过去。以他的说法，我是一个未来的自己，具有远较大的知识，然而，他用那知识来改变他当前的实相：而当我是鲁柏时，我并没有那知识。那么，你可以说，我正在改变我自己的过去。但鲁柏目前的经验也改变了我目前的经验——所以，有一个无穷尽的交流。", "en": "(Leaning forward, speaking intently but half-humorously:) I have memories of being Ruburt — but the Ruburt I was is not the Ruburt that Ruburt is in his reality. He surprises me, and his reactions alter my past. In his terms I am a future self, with far greater knowledge, yet he uses that knowledge to alter his present reality; and when I was Ruburt I did not have that knowledge. You can say then that I am altering my own past, but Ruburt’s present experience also changes my present experience — and so there is an unending interchange.5", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第728节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "728", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1748", "zh": "我并不是指那重聚是不可避免的或注定的，但你可以说，那可能性的活力放大了原始的张力。不论是就创作上的努力或身体的情况而言，我要鲁柏将所有这些应用在他自己的情况上，因此他会开始了解，他能在现在开始对一个未来的复原反应。", "en": "I do not mean that the reunion was inevitable or predestined, but the vigor of that probability, you might say, magnified the original tension. I want Ruburt to apply all of this to his own situation, both in terms of creative endeavors and his physical situation, so that he begins to understand that he can start to react in the present to a future recovery.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第13节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "13", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1792", "zh": "你的梦的确是有关改变过去及过去信念的，所以，是有关插入一个新现在和一个新未来。头发往往是力量的一个象征，但在这例子里，它代表旧信念的力量，而你的父亲是剪掉那些的理发师——反之他在过去遵守许多相当负面的信念和观念。杰克也代表你自己一般有关工作的任何信念，它能带你这么远而已，不能再远了。你正确地诠释鲁柏和他母亲之间的事——附带一句，一个极佳的预兆。", "en": "Your dream did indeed deal with changing the past and the past beliefs, and therefore with inserting a new present, and a newer future. Often hair is a symbol for strength, but in this case it represents the strength of old beliefs, and your father is a barber who cuts away those — whereas in the past he followed many quite negative beliefs and concepts. Jake also represented any beliefs of your own dealing with work in general that can carry you so far and no further. You correctly interpreted the affair between Ruburt and his mother — an excellent omen, by the way.", "source": "健康之道 · 第2节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "2", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "当下看起来卡死的时候，怎么松开它", "note": "常见的困境是：看自己、看世界，被目前的状态催眠到以为一切改变和成长都不可能。赛斯给过几把钥匙。其一，过去的期望虽然对你有影响，但不足以绑住当世的人格——别拿过去当判决书。其二，与过去那些有生产力或喜悦的时期连结，对当下有直接的作用，正面暗示和负面暗示一样在起作用。其三，警惕把恐惧的画面投射到眼前的事件上：有人把害怕的图景盖在当下，身体就做出反映混乱的行动；同样，在被天然安全的处境里被想象出来的危险吓到，是因为你分不清身体上目前安全的状况与想象中的不安全。其四，给注意力做操：想象你完全在世界的另一部分，但仍在现在这个时刻，问自己同样的问题，再回看前一天、或把你自己搁在一周之后——这些练习教的东西没法解释，它给你的是一种关于自己的感觉。最后是态度问题：那些教人消灭欲望、灭绝自我的玄秘门派，牺牲掉的恰恰是你每一个片刻的宝贵直接性——当下不是要被超越的障碍，它是你唯一的入口。", "src": "早期课第2册第 76 节；早期课第7册第 281 节；《心灵的本质》第 752、793、799 节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第 805 节；《神奇之道》第 5 节；《健康之道》第 3 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 76 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 281 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 752 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 793 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 799 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 805 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 5 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 3 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0255", "zh": "这是非常有价值的资讯，特别是有关期望在过滤可用资料上扮演的角色。期望也有点受到前世的影响，但程度不足以绑住当世的人格。", "en": "This is extremely valuable information, particularly concerning the part played by expectation in the sifting of available data. Expectation is somewhat influenced also by past existences, and yet not enough to be binding upon the present personality.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第76节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "76", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0695", "zh": "发掘你的潜意识有何感觉，摆锤是一个绝佳的方法，而不是改变它们。顺便说一下，如你们两人所知，从几个观点看来，你今天晚上播放的音乐非常有益（伊玛·苏马克[Yma Sumac]）。与过去充满生产力或喜悦的时期有关的任何连结，都和当下有直接的关系。就像负面的暗示有它们的作用一样，正面的暗示也是，而且两者都是就象征而言。", "en": "The pendulum is an excellent method of discovering your subconscious feelings, and indeed of changing them. As you both suppose, incidentally, the music you played this evening was highly beneficial from several standpoints. (Yma Sumac.) Any connection with past periods of productivity or joy have immediate reference to the present. As negative suggestions play their part, so do positive suggestions, and both in terms of symbols.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第281节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "281", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1541", "zh": "在个人的生活里以及世界的舞台上，行动一直在发生中。你很容易就可以看看你自己或看看世界。看见你自己是如此地被你目前的状态所催眠，以致所有的改变或成长似乎都不可能；或看见世界也是同样的情形。", "en": "In private life and on the world stage, action is occurring all the time. It is easy to look at yourselves or at the world, comma, to see yourself and become so hypnotized by your present state that all change or growth seems impossible, or to see the world in the same manner.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第752节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "752", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1593", "zh": "另一个练习是，想象你完全在世界的另一部分，但却在现在这个时刻，而问你自己同样的问题。为了变化起见，以你的心眼追随你自己前一天的活动。或把你自己搁在一周之后。指挥你自己这些练习的变奏。它们将教你什么是无法解释的，因为它们将提供一个经验的次元，一个对你自己的感觉，那可能只有你懂得。", "en": "For another exercise, imagine that you are in another part of the world entirely, but in present time, and ask yourself the same questions. For variety, in your mind’s eye follow your own activities of the previous day. Place yourself a week ahead in time. Conduct your own variations of these exercises. What they will teach you cannot be explained, for they will provide a dimension of experience, a feeling about yourself that may make sense only to you.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第793节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "793", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1604", "zh": "你有意识的心智是为着给你的身体一个估量，这估量可称之为文化状况，因为以你们的话来说，有些世事的成熟度和特点只有意识才能评估。如果，在以主要经验来说是自然地安全的状况下，你被来自次要经验——那就是说，由阅读或不论什么——的不安全信号吓坏了——你表现出缺乏辨识力。你不能分辨身体上目前安全的状况，与那想象中也许是不安全的情况，而导致了危险的警号。", "en": "Your conscious mind is meant to give your body an assessment of what I will call cultural conditions, for there are sophistications and specifications that in your terms consciousness alone can assess. If, under conditions naturally safe in the terms of primary experience, you become overwhelmed by unsafe signals from secondary experience — that is, from your reading or whatever — you show a lack of discrimination. You are not able to differentiate between the physically safe present situation, and the imagined, which is perhaps unsafe, calling forth the alarms of danger.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第799节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "799", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1620", "zh": "在此许多复辟的玄秘学派都推崇欲望的死亡、自我的灭绝，以便把物质元素变炼到一个更精细的层面。在所有这些例子当中，个人清晰的心灵与生物的健全性受到蒙蔽，而无法把握当下这宝贵的一刻。", "en": "Many of your resurrected occult schools speak of a recommended death of desire, the annihilation of the ego, for the transmutation of physical elements to finer levels. In all such cases the clear spiritual and biological integrity of the individual suffers, and the precious immediacy of your moments is largely lost.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第805节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "805", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1740", "zh": "当然，他已自标的处完全移转了他的注意力。他曾将他恐惧的画面，而非他原先意图的画面，投射在目前的事件上。他的身体响应他的心象和他的思维，带来反映他的迷惑的行动。", "en": "He has switched his attention from the target, of course, completely. He has projected upon the present event the picture of his fears, rather than the picture of his original intent. His body, responding to his mental images and his thoughts, brings out actions that mirror his confusion.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第5节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "5", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1806", "zh": "如果你试着将所有这些潜意识记忆一直保持在脑海中最重要的地方，那么，你真的会根本无法在当下片刻思考或行动。不过，你对你自己的潜意识心智，的确多少有某个通路。也许，想象一个意识的连续体要容易得多，因为，你也有一个身体意识，而那身体意识本身是由形成身体所有部分的每个分子之个别意识所组成的。", "en": "If you tried to hold all of those subconscious memories uppermost in your mind all of the time, then you would literally be unable to think or act in the present moment at all. You do more or less have a certain access to your own subconscious mind, however. It is perhaps easier to imagine a continuum of consciousness, for you have a body consciousness also, and that body consciousness is itself made up of the individual consciousness of each molecule that forms all parts of the body itself.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "怎么进入它，以及哪些能力根植于它", "note": "方法在第 78 节，朴素得意外：一次在广阔当下与大自然里的感官沉浸就能让你们焕然一新，靠的是情感上的接纳——越是用意识死死专注（比如硬做心理时间练习），越不见效。门槛却并不低：第 277 节说极少数情况下你可以有效投射到觉知广阔的现在，那时你会同时感到所有系统的实相，但经验的记忆很可能留不住；第 287 节说强度的高峰可以让你感知它，可若没有合适的根本假设，你并不会理解自己感知到的东西。第 289 节解释「为什么带不回来」：内在感官在广阔的现在里处理基本资料，回来后必须按物理时间架构重新解释，所以「时间混乱」总是存在，有机体得自己形成中和的保护机制。第 305 节说原因很硬：肉体头脑装不下无限的概念，只有全我、内我能像你在空间中行动那样在无限里移动。晚期口述（《梦、进化与价值完成》第 884 节）仍在交代同一个方法：借心智练习跃过传统的事件架构，以知性与直觉一起，感觉你自己在「大到能包含所有时间片段的宽阔现在」里的那一部分。\n\n为什么内在感官能「知道」外在自我没见到的东西？因为它们的根基在这里。第 239 节：心智（对比大脑）以广阔的现在的方式感知时间，它的联想不只来自过去，也来自未来。第 120 节：千里眼存在且可能，因为它的根基就在广阔的现在之内——这类内在资料持续自动地被人类架构的每一部分接受，除了外在自我；连外在自我也常在不自知的情况下据它行动，并因此免于悲惨境地。第 121 节：心智与广阔的现在紧密结合。梦是日常的通道：第 93 节说一个梦允许内我在广阔的现在之内观照它自己，而肉体要存活就必须做梦；第 115 节把梦世界放得更近，第 49 节则断言梦世界及其持续性一直都在广阔的现在之内。第 287 节把它扩到艺术（还玩了个双关）：广阔的现在「总是 present」在任何一件作品里——流动性弥漫在具象与抽象的画作、也弥漫在梦状态中，意象由做梦者按自己的理解投射进去。第 301 节顺手解释了星光层：那不过是广阔现在更大的部分跨越你们的时间扭曲而显现出来的、你们意识上不熟悉的实相。", "src": "早期课第2册第 49、78 节；早期课第3册第 93、115、120、121 节；早期课第5册第 239 节；早期课第6册第 277 节；早期课第7册第 287、289、301、305 节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第 884 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 49 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 78 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 93 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 115 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 120 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 121 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 239 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 277 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 287 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 289 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 301 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 305 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 884 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "方法、门槛、带不回来的原因", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0258", "zh": "你们现在也正在做这件事。鲁柏现在正在这么做。你最近做心理时间的成效不显著，很大一部分原因出于你用太多意识专注在这件事情上。一种情感上的接纳就是答案，这一点在鲁柏听来也许不以为然，再说一次，在无限广阔的现在和大自然里的一次感官上的沉浸，将使你们焕然一新。", "en": "You are doing so now. Ruburt is doing so now. Your lack of success lately with psychological time has been to a large measure caused by too great a conscious concentration upon the task. An emotional acceptance, distasteful as this may seem to Ruburt, is the answer here, and again a sensual immersion in the spacious present and in nature will refresh you here.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0691", "zh": "在极少数情况下，要是幸运的话，你是可以如此有效地旅行或投射，而觉知广阔的现在，在这种状况下，你会同时感觉到所有系统的实相。但是这里有一个很大的可能性是，整个经验的记忆不会保留下来。", "en": "On very few occasions you may, if you are lucky, travel or project so effectively that you are aware of the spacious present, in which case you will sense the reality of all systems simultaneously. But here there is a strong possibility that memory of the experience in its entirety will not be retained.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第277节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "277", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0702", "zh": "如果思想在场的话，它们是不会被感知到的，你看。然而，如果这里达到了某一个强度，一个强度的高峰，那么你就可能感知到广阔的现在，就像它存在于你的原生系统之内那样。理论上，你可能从那个高峰探究另一个系统，但你不会了解你感知的东西。你不会有合适的根本假设，你知道。", "en": "The thoughts would not be perceived if they were present, you see. If a certain intensity is reached here however, a peak of intensity, then you could perceive the spacious present as it exists within your native system. You could, from this peak, theoretically look into the other system, but you would not understand what you perceived. You would not have the proper root assumptions, you see.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第287节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "287", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0709", "zh": "时间混乱（time scramble）总是有的，因为内在感官是在广阔的现在与基本资料打交道，一个中和的元素将会发展出来，保护鲁柏免于前几天晚上他所经历的那种情感电荷的全面冲击。有机体本身形成这个自我保护机制。", "en": "There is always a time scramble, for the inner senses deal with basic data in the spacious present . Then the data must be interpreted in the time scheme of physical existence. (Long pause.) With training and experience a neutralizing element will be developed that protects Ruburt against the full Emotional charge that he experienced the other evening. The organism itself forms this as a self protective mechanism.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第289节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "289", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0738", "zh": "一方面，所有的自己都是整体或当下所是（that which is）的投射。新的宇宙，比如你们自己的宇宙，持续不断进入存在中。迥异的系统和层面发展出来，进而形成其他系统。只有从主观和心灵的角度来说，无限才有意义。肉体的头脑无法容纳无限的概念。 这个概念与三维的说法不相容。全我、内我在无限的概念之内移动，就像你在物质实相的空间之中行动一样。无限包含未来成为已知的一切，当然，未来将成为已知的一切在广阔的现在之内是已知的。", "en": "Now, in one sense, all selves are projections of the whole or that which is. New universes such as your own constantly come into existence. Systems and planes far different develop and in turn form other systems. Infinity has meaning only in subjective and psychic terms. The physical brain cannot contain the idea of infinity. The concept will not fit into three dimensional terms. The whole self, the inner self moves within the concept of infinity as you move within physical reality through space. Infinity contains all that will ever be known, and, of course, all that will ever be known is known within the spacious present .", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第305节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "305", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1654", "zh": "我们依然称我们下一章为，把某些事件以顺序的形式罗列给你们。希望在此书其它部分的某些精神练习，会容许你们跃过传统的事件架构，而以统合的知性及直觉，感觉你自己个人存在于一个“宽阔的现在”的那部分，这宽阔的现在是大到能包含所有时间的片断的。", "en": "We will nevertheless call our next chapter “In the Beginning,” laying certain events out for you in serial form. I hope that in other portions of this book certain mental exercises will allow you to leap over the tradition of time’s framework and sense with the united intellect and intuitions your own individual part in a spacious present that is large enough to contain all of time’s segments.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第884节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "884", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "根植于它的能力：心智、千里眼、梦、画", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0197", "zh": "我一直想要谈这件事，因为我可以向你们证明这个梦世界的存在，以及它的持续性，一直都在广阔的现在之内。你们必须先了解心理实相、心理时间、心理经验，还有梦存在，才能学会运用很多能力，因为在以上提过的所有面向中，你们是在潜意识层使用你们的能力，也就是你们的内在感官。", "en": "I have wanted to cover this because I can prove the existence of this dream world to you, and its continuity, always within the spacious present. You must understand psychological reality, psychological time, psychological experience, and the dream existence before you can learn to utilize many abilities, since in all the mentioned aspects, you use your abilities, that is your inner senses, on a subconscious level.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第49节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "49", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0300", "zh": "换句话说，一个梦允许内我在广阔的现在之内观照它自己。现在，在化学上肉体的确需要做梦。也就是说，如果肉体要存活，就必须做梦。这是某些化学反应和必要的化学物，也就是白天累积的多余化学物，激发心智的梦机制而造成的结果。", "en": "In other words, a dream allows the inner self to view itself within the spacious present. Now, chemically the physical body does need to dream. That is, dreaming is a necessity if the physical body is to survive. This is the result of certain chemical reactions and chemical necessities, chemical excesses that build up during the days, inciting the mental dream mechanism.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第93节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "93", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0343", "zh": "这样的发展意味着，多余的能量释放到你们的场域而得以利用，在各个方向都有无止尽的可能性。意念和观念是吸引未结盟的能量，指挥和集中它的非物质现实。梦世界更近距离存在于内我非常有觉察的那个广阔的现在里。它和伪装建构的关系不像它和你们自己的宇宙那么紧密，而且它的反应有点受制于它自己的架构之内。", "en": "Such developments would mean the releasing and availability of added energy into your field, that would have endless possibilities in all directions. Ideas and concepts are nonphysical actualities that attract unaligned energy, direct and concentrate it. The dream world exists more closely in that spacious present of which the inner self is so aware. It is not as involved with camouflage constructions as your own universe, and its actions are somewhat limited within its own framework.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0351", "zh": "千里眼是存在而且是可能的，因为它的基础在广阔的现在之内，这之所以不为人知，是因为人类不会接受可得的资料。千里眼存在，因为物质和能量是同一件事。在肉体本身的器官之内有千里眼，因为身体的器官不“只是”物质，而是能量把它自己组成物质。这样的内在资料持续而且自动被人类架构的每一个其他部分接受，除了外在自我以外。甚至这个外在自我，话说回来，也在毫不知情的状况下，经常根据它不承认它接收到的这类资讯而行动；而且这样的行动往往把它从悲惨状况中解救出来。", "en": "Clairvoyance exists and is possible because of its basis within the spacious present, and this is not known because man will not accept the available data. Clairvoyance exists because matter and energy are one and the same thing. There is clairvoyance within the organs of the physical body itself, because the organs of the body are not, quote, “just” matter, but energy which has composed itself into matter. Such inner data continually and automatically is accepted by every other portion of the human framework except by the outer ego. Even this outer ego, however, acts all unknowingly often on the basis of such information, which it will not admit it has received; and often such action saves it from dire circumstances.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第120节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "120", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0353", "zh": "你们将会发现心智和广阔的现在紧密结合在一起。如果去研究的话，心智的能力会引导人类认识我谈过的这些其他的现实场域。心智和无形之物打交道，但它不和非实相打交道。再说一次，一个现实的效力并不光是由它在物质之内的外观决定，物质的成分最初是无形的成分，而研究心智以及研究心智创造其梦形象的过程，可能因此对人类在潜意识中制造他自己实质宇宙的物质形象有基本的了解。", "en": "The mind will be found to be closely allied with the spacious present. The mind’s capabilities, if studied, would lead man into a realization of these other fields of actuality of which I have spoken. The mind deals with intangibles, but it does not deal with unrealities. Again, the validity of an actuality is not to be determined by its appearance within matter alone. The ingredients of matter are first of all intangible ingredients, and the study of the mind and a study of the processes by which the mind creates its dream images could lead to a basic understanding of the manner in which man subconsciously produces the physical images of his own material universe.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第121节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "121", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0594", "zh": "现在。对比于大脑，心智以一种广阔的现在来感知时间。这是真的，心智是以联想原则来运行。因此这些不只是从过去，也会从未来而来。", "en": "Now. The mind as opposed to the brain, perceives time in terms of the spacious present. It is true that the mind works on associative principles. Therefore these associations are drawn not only from the past, but also from the future.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第239节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "239", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0704", "zh": "广阔的现在一直都在（微笑）——我的双关语——在任何艺术作品之中。你应该知道，具象画与抽象画各有不同的流动形态。流动性或广阔的现在普遍弥漫在梦状态中，就像它在画作中一样，但是做梦者按照他自己的了解与经验，把意象投射到广阔的现在。", "en": "The spacious present is always present(smile)—my pun—in any work of art. As you should know, there is a difference in the type of mobility of an objective painting, and an abstract one. The fluidity or the spacious present pervades the dream state as it pervades a painting, but the images are projected into the spacious present by the dreamer, according to his own understanding and experience.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第287节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "287", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0725", "zh": "当你觉察到行动的更大维度时，你就会对人格是什么更有觉知。我告诉过你，你存在的维度比你知道的还多。现在，有些人称这些为星光层（astral planes,或译为灵界）。它们只是代表你在意识上不熟悉的实相而已，它们也跨越你们的时间元素当中种种的扭曲，好让广阔的现在显现出更大的部分。", "en": "As you become aware of the larger dimensions of action, so you will become more aware of what personality is. I have told you that you exist in more dimensions than you know. Now, these have been referred to by some as astral planes. They simply represent realities with which you are not consciously familiar, and they span the distortions of your time elements so that larger portions of the spacious present become apparent.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第301节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "301", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B11", "title": "生死、并存的生命，与持续不断的创造", "note": "广阔的现在最实用的两个推论：死亡不是出口，转世不是排队。第 96 节：要是所有实相不在广阔的现在里同时存在，能量出现在一个形式里就可以说将结束在那个形式里——正因为有它，人格可以穿越各个不同的实相。第 48 节：生前就学会认清广阔的现在，死亡经验就没那么可怕，自我不会被突如其来的感知吓住——就在死亡之前，无时间开始被感知，而被吓坏的自我通常选择躲进过去。第 425 节：对你们系统之外的存在来说，出生与死亡这种「计时」毫无意义。第 256 节把「同时」讲透：各个独立的存在同时发生，区分时间的只有自我；坚持用本身错误的时间理论去想转世才会处处矛盾，必须按对广阔现在的了解来想。第 312 节解开「为何只记得前世」的死结：以肉体生物的存在你们无法记得未来，所以想得起来的只有过去世——然而在梦状态里，所谓未来世的存在早已不陌生，对内在感官而言前生来世全部同时。第 256、407 节留下一个私人注脚：在广阔的现在里「我们是一体，但又完全是个体」，珍与赛斯都生活在其中；第 428 节补：因为广阔的现在，这些自己其实同时处在一切地方，你接近某个次元，就是接近某一时刻的一个人格。\n\n最后把镜头拉回全景：广阔的现在也是创造的舞台。第 147 节：之前之后只是为了你们方便的说法，实际只有所有行动在广阔的现在之内，从它自己中自发地、朝四面八方涌出，自行形成一切无限的现实场域与系统。第 112 节：一切物质都是客观化的精神行动，基本上同时发生在广阔的现在。第 248 节：广阔的现在包含所有系统，而组成它们的能量是同一个，所以看似封闭的系统其实全是开放系统。第 303 节：纵使一切总在「变为」的状态中，在广阔的现在里「一切万有确实存在」——变为永远不会完成，但你无论在哪里画线，都会把它想成终点。晚期口述把模型总结到位：《梦、进化与价值完成》第 897 节说那是一个「经常不断的创造」，创造持续、自发、在每个地方同时发生，「在一种广阔的现在里，所有我们对时间的经验都是从那里浮现出来的」；第 886 节把它推到神圣层——最初是一个神圣的心理完形，存在于一个心理次元、一个广阔的现在，其中所有过去、现在或未来的一切，都被保持在同一个灿烂的多重眷注的焦点里。", "src": "早期课第2册第 48 节；早期课第3册第 96、112、147 节；早期课第6册第 248、256 节；早期课第7册第 303、312 节；早期课第8册第 407 节；早期课第9册第 425、428 节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第 886、897 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 48 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 96 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 112 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 147 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 248 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 256 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 303 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 312 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 407 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 425 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 428 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 886 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 897 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "死亡不是出口，转世不是排队", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0191", "zh": "心理时间的运用将使死亡的经验不那么可怕。到时候，你们已经学会认清什么是广阔的现在，而意识自我也不会因为突如其来的感知而那么不知所措和困惑不安。", "en": "The use of psychological time will make the experience of death much less frightening. You will already have learned to recognize the spacious present for what it is, and the conscious ego will not be so bewildered and confused by the sudden perception that is involved.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第48节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "48", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0192", "zh": "就在死亡经验之前，无时间或广阔的现在开始被感知。那是因为自我被过去束缚，所以它看见过去似乎历历在目。可以这么说，它有能力看见即将到来的事，但是当那被吓坏的自我仍然掌控时，它选择只看一部分可能发生的事，而在死亡的一刻来临之前，它通常选择躲在过去。", "en": "Just before the experience of death, timelessness, or the spacious present, begins to be perceived. It is because the ego is tied to its past that it sees the past seemingly rise up. It has the ability to see what is coming, so to speak, but while the frightened ego is still in control it chooses to see only a portion of what is possible, and before the point of death it usually chooses to hide in the past.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第48节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "48", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0315", "zh": "实相融合，一个融入另一个之中。人格，任何类型的个体化能量，可以穿越各个不同的实相。要不是有广阔的现在存在 —— 其中所有实相都是同时的 —— 那么能量出现在一个形式之中，就可以说是，将结束在那个形式之中。", "en": "Realities merge, one into the other. Personalities, or any type of individualized energy, may pass through various realities. The appearance of energy in one form could be said to end in that form were it not for the existence of the spacious present, in which all realities are simultaneous.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第96节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "96", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0633", "zh": "一方面，自己通常被想成是，只存在一个特定的时间顺序模式之内。然而，当你想到未来时，它的经验却是根源于过去。由于实际上只有一个广阔的现在，所以这意味着，按照你们的说法，自己既根源于过去也根源于未来。", "en": "For one thing the self is usually thought of in terms of existence only within one particular time sequence pattern. Its experience however is rooted in the past, as you think of the past. Since there is actually only a spacious present this means that the self is rooted both in the past and in the future, using your terms.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第256节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "256", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0634", "zh": "我承认，转世似乎确实有这样的含义。这只是因为你们坚持根据本身不正确的时间理论来思考转世。反之，你们必须根据你们对广阔现在的了解来思考转世。", "en": "I admit to you reincarnation does seem to have such implications. This is simply because you insist upon considering reincarnation in the light of time theories that are themselves incorrect. You must instead consider reincarnation in the light of what you know of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第256节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "256", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0636", "zh": "事实上，你看，这些个别的存在同时发生。区分时间的只有自我而已。你感知不到各个存在，或者不如说，同时存在自我感知不到它们。基本上，你知道，过骈、现在和未来同时存在于广阔的现在之中。", "en": "In actuality you see, these separate existences occur simultaneously. It is only the ego who makes the time distinction. The various existences are not perceivable by you, or rather they are not perceivable to the ego. In a basic manner, as you know, the past, present and future exist at once in the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第256节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "256", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0644", "zh": "现在。我就是你所属的主要本体。而且我自己曾经是，可以说，另一个主要本体的一部分。由于很多原因，这种发展并不是经常会发生。一些本体的片段体根本不希望这样发展。在广阔的现在中，你会发现我们是一体，但又完全是个体。", "en": "Now. I am the prime identity that you were part of. And I was myself at one time, so to speak, a part of another prime identity. This development does not always occur, for many reasons. Some fragments of an identity simply do not wish to so develop. In the spacious present you see we are one, yet entirely individual.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第256节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "256", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0755", "zh": "在广阔的现在，根本没有这种事情。其他的自己，在物质系统之内以物质生物的形式转世，和你们一样体验时间是一个衔接着另一个的一连串时刻。在梦中以及在出神状态里的记忆通常已经被审查过了。单单以肉体生物的形式存在，你们是无法记得未来的。因此想得起来的只有过去世而已。然而在梦状态中，在你看来是未来世的存在其实早已不陌生。对内在感官而言，这些前世与来生全部同时存在。", "en": "In the spacious present there are no such terms. Other selves, reincarnated within the physical system as physical creatures, experienced time as you do, as a series of moments strung out one before the other. Memories in dreams and in the trance state are usually already censored. As physical creatures alone you cannot remember the future. Therefore only past lives are ever recalled. In the dream state however what would appear to you as future lives are already familiar. To the inner senses all of these existences are simultaneous.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第312节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "312", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0851", "zh": "赛斯就是我所是的，但我比赛斯所是的还多。赛斯是独立的（微笑，睁开眼睛），随着我不断发展，他也继续发展。（微笑）你也知道，我们两个都生活在广阔的现在中。", "en": "Seth is what I am, and yet I am more than Seth is. Seth is however independent (smile, eyes open), and continues to develop as I continue to develop also. (Smile.) In the spacious present you see, we both exist.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第407节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "407", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0876", "zh": "广袤的现在对你们系统之外的存在而言，是一个生动鲜活得多的实相。对个人来说，你们的时间似乎由出生与死亡来标记。当出生与死亡被认识为它们的本来面目，当人格能够随意改变形相时，这种所谓“计时”便毫无意义了。", "en": "The spacious present is much more a vivid reality to those outside of your system. Your time seems marked, individually, by birth and death. When these are known for what they are, when the personality can change form at will, such quote “timing” is meaningless.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第425节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "425", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0888", "zh": "换句话说，因为广袤的现在是存在的，这些自己其实同时处在一切地方。然而，当你似乎接近不同的次元时，你就似乎接近了这样一个人格：他存在于你感知他的那个时刻。", "en": "Now because the spacious present exists, in other terms, these selves are actually in all places at one time. As you seem to approach different dimensions however, then you seem to approach a personality who exists at the time of your perception of him.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第428节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "428", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "创造：持续、自发、同时", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-035-e0339", "zh": "既然你们对物质的本质略知一二，就会明白所有的物质都是客观化的精神行动，基本上这样的行动同时发生在广阔的现在，是由个体化能量透过精神围场的成形而形成的。", "en": "Now that you know something about the nature of matter, you will see that all matter is objectified mental action, and that basically such action happens simultaneously in the spacious present, formed by individualized energy through the formation of mental enclosures.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第112节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "112", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0396", "zh": "再一次在这里，当我说之前和之后的时候，我说的只是为了你们的方便，因为没有之前也没有之后，有的只是所有行动都在广阔的现在之内，发生在它自己之外，自发地，进入四面八方，自行形成所有无限的现实场域和系统。", "en": "Again here, when I speak in terms of before and after, I speak only for your convenience, for there is no before or after, only all action within the spacious present, occurring out of itself, spontaneously, into all directions, and forming of itself all the infinite fields and systems of actuality.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第147节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "147", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0619", "zh": "广阔的现在显然也包含所有这些系统，这些系统全部都是开放的系统，因为组成它们的能量是相同的。它们看起来是封闭的系统，我们改天会深入讨论这一个问题。", "en": "Now the spacious present obviously contains all of these systems, and these systems are all open systems, for the energy that composes them is the same. They appear to be closed systems, and we shall go more deeply into this particular matter upon another occasion.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第248节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "248", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e0735", "zh": "而是一直在一种变为的状态中。然而在广阔的现在，一切万有确实存在。变为永远都不会完成，但是无论你选择在哪里画一条线，你都会把它想成是一个终点。", "en": "But always in a state of becoming. However in the Spacious present , All That Is does exist. The becoming can never be completed and yet wherever you choose to draw a line, you will think of it as an end.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第303节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "303", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1659", "zh": "反之，在最初，再次的，是有个神圣的心理完形（gestalt）——我是指一个存在，其实相不能以“存在”（being）这个字来定义，因为它就是所有存在由之而出的那个来源。那个存在存在于一个心理的次元（长长的停顿），一个广阔的现在，在其中所有过去、现在或未来的一切东西全都保持在它的密切注意里，在一个神圣的范畴里安立不动——这范畴是在这样一个灿烂的关注里，以致最伟大和最低下的、最大和最小的，都同等的在一个多重眷爱的不变焦点里。", "en": "In the beginning there was instead, once more, a divine psychological gestalt—and by that I mean a being whose reality escapes the definition of the word “being,” since it is the source from which all being emerges. That being exists in a psychological dimension (long pause), a spacious present, in which everything that was or is or will be (in your terms) is kept in immediate attention, poised in a divine context that is characterized (long pause, eyes closed) by such a brilliant concentration that the grandest and the lowliest, the largest and the smallest, are equally held in a multiloving constant focus.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第886节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "886", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-035-e1675", "zh": "可是，整体而言，虽然我必须以系列性的讲法来解释它，但我们说的是一个经常不断的创造。我们在讨论一个宇宙的模型，在其中，创造是继续的、自发的，并且同时的在每个地方发生。在一种广阔的现在里，所有我们对时间的经验都是从那里浮现出来的。在这个模型里，永远有新的能量，而所有的系统都是开放的，纵使它们看起来也许是分别的运作。再一次的，这个模型也建立它每个部分之主动的合作上，那些部分以某种方式也参与了整体的经验。", "en": "All in all, however, we are speaking of a constant creation, even though I must explain it in serial terms. We are discussing a model of the universe in which creation is continuous, spontaneously occurring everywhere, and everywhere simultaneously, in a kind of spacious present, from which all experiences with time emerge. In this model there is always new energy, and all systems are open, even though they may seem to operate separately. Once again, also, we are considering a model that is based upon the active cooperation of each of its parts, which in one way or another also participate in the experience of the whole.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第897节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "897", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 19}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 17}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 12}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 11}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 6}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 5}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 4}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 4}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 4}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 3}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 2}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 2}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 2}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 2}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 11, "quotes": 118, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 31}};
